// =====================================================================
// ProjectDelivery — the SelfSync delivery backlog (backfilled 2026-07-04, D0004). The shipped
// milestones (M1-M6, the goal-#1 config-UX overhaul, the 0.6.0 fix set) are DONE tasks, each
// with a method-tagged DoD Test + an appended pass TestResult (judged at the backfill commit;
// the automated suites are green at HEAD). The outstanding backlog (B7/B9/B11 + the L3/L4
// verification gaps) are OPEN tasks — a DoD criterion with NO pass result yet, so `keel orient`
// reports them as the ready/outstanding frontier. Results are APPENDED, never edited.
// =====================================================================
package ProjectDelivery {
    private import EngineElement::*;
    private import EngineWork::*;
    private import EngineVerification::*;
    private import ProjectBusiness::*; // nConfigSync — the Need the config-sync capability derives from

    action def SelfSyncDelivery {
        // ---- open backlog (NOT done) ----
        // Follow-up to changeProvenanceNotify (1.18.0): notify on a peer's config/plugin DELETION too. The
        // source-driven notice covers add/edit changes (they carry provenance); a DELETION does not, because
        // the Deletion wire type has no author/device fields. Extending it needs Deletion provenance on the
        // server + a delete-path notice on the client. Triages issueDeletionProvenanceUnnotified (open).
        action deletionProvenanceNotify;
        // ---- shipped milestones (DONE) ----
        action m1Protocol;          // M1: auth + changes/get/put/delete + WS, two-client propagation
        action m2ChunkingBinary;    // M2: content-defined chunking, content-addressed store, binary+dedup
        action m3ConflictMerge;     // M3: base-aware reconcile, diff3 three-way merge, conflict-copy
        action m4MultiTenant;       // M4: accounts (argon2id) + named vaults, vault-scoped routes
        action m5Mobile;            // M5: mobile-safe paths — isDesktopOnly:false, requestUrl, pure-TS chunker
        action m6Packaging;         // M6: BRAT packaging + release workflow + Docker/reverse-proxy
        action goal1ConfigUx;       // goal #1: setup wizard + status-first grouped settings
        action rel06FixSet;         // 0.6.0: vault-switch resolution, single indicator, settings reorg
        action testHardeningClient; // Phase 1 (D0026): close the client imperative-edge test gaps the audit found. Real transport.ts unit tests (CAS 409/404→CommitConflictError, 30s timeout race, errText, the diagnose() ladder, login mustChange) over a controllable requestUrl; first tests for the 4 previously-zero-coverage UI modules (vaultswitch destructive mirror/fork flows incl. the SF1 read-only-with-local-data-must-prompt guard, confirm dismissal semantics, devicelink no-password-in-link, configdir first-contact direction); merge3 EOL/conflict/large-input tests; fixed the tautological https-not-refused test. CAUGHT + FIXED a MEDIUM defect: merge3 CRLF normalization (issueMergeCrlf). Coverage is COMPUTED + floored (D0026), not attested.
        action testHardeningServer; // Phase 2 (D0026): close the server orchestration/concurrency test gaps. New tests/ws.rs — first WebSocket integration suite (subprotocol-token auth valid/missing/garbage/empty, per-user cap → 503, global-reserve rollback, ConnGuard teardown counter → 0, revoke-mid-session, must_change gate); drove ws.rs 13.5%→76% line coverage with the ConnGuard/counter invariants directly asserted (no leak, no cap bypass). New tests/hardening.rs — concurrent-commit CAS race (exactly one 200/one 409), DoS bounds (oversized chunk 400, body 413, 10k-hash cap 400), degraded-storage 503-not-empty-manifest contract, vaults-per-user cap, corrupt-JSON-store fail-loud, api.rs 403/404/409 mapping + idempotent leave/delete. Fixed the flaky env-mutating config_defaults_and_env test (serialized on a Mutex, env saved/restored). Server line coverage 86.4%→90.0%. No server defects found — primitives were sound, the gap was purely untested concurrency/WS/bounds.
        action realObsidianE2eSmoke; // Phase 3 (D0026): the real-Obsidian e2e layer the headless suite structurally can't cover. A Playwright+CDP harness (client/e2e-obsidian/) launches an ISOLATED real Obsidian instance (pre-seeded obsidian.json vault registry + fixed --remote-debugging-port + connectOverCDP, so it never touches a running Obsidian), opens a staged vault with the freshly-built plugin auto-enabled, and asserts END-TO-END: the plugin constructs (real ObsidianVaultIo + requestUrl glue loads), auto-connects from persisted settings, and a seeded note actually SYNCS to a real spawned server (serverHasFile). Ported/adapted from origin/test_real_obsidian. LOCAL/NIGHTLY gate — needs Obsidian installed, so not in per-PR CI (specs self-skip when absent); `npm run test:obsidian-e2e`. Verified green locally (5-12s). The harness supports fuller scenarios (two-device convergence, conflict, status UI) as follow-ups.
        action realObsidianE2eMultiDevice; // Phase 3 expansion (D0026): TWO-DEVICE convergence through real Obsidian — the core SelfSync promise the headless suite + single-device smoke can't show. Parameterized the CDP launcher port so two ISOLATED Obsidian instances run concurrently (distinct ports + user-data-dirs), both syncing one server vault; renderer helpers create/modify/read notes via the real app.vault (firing genuine file events). convergence.pwspec.ts asserts BIDIRECTIONAL: a note made on device A reaches device B, AND a change on B flows back to A, plus both plugins reach a healthy (non-offline) status. Green locally (~13-20s). Deliberately NOT a live divergent-conflict test: forcing a deterministic conflict through two auto-syncing GUIs is flaky, and the conflict LOGIC (3-way merge, conflict-copy) is already covered headlessly (reconcile.test + integration-matrix). Local/nightly gate.
        action postOverhaulHardening; // Post-overhaul backlog (D0026 follow-on): two maintenance fixes. (1) Bumped vitest + @vitest/coverage-v8 2.1.9→3.2.7 so the full `--coverage` run works on Node 24 (v2.1.9 predated Node 24; its v8 provider crashed nondeterministically under fileParallelism:false). All 388 tests pass under the major bump, all coverage floors hold — verified locally EXIT 0. (2) Removed the baked SYNC_USER/SYNC_PASSWORD from the server Dockerfile ENV (SecretsUsedInArgOrEnv — a password in ENV persists into image layers); code defaults + boot weak-password guard unchanged, creds now provided at runtime. Resolves issueDockerfileEnvSecret.
        action falseAbsenceDeleteFix; // Data-safety (D0047, issueFalseAbsenceDelete): a delete-remote must never fire on mere absence-from-the-listing. reconcile.ts delete-remote now requires CONFIRMED absence via a direct per-path probe (confirmedAbsent: io.exists, else a read — never the fallible io.list()); a file that's absent from the listing but still readable/existing (a failed directory enumeration, or an unhydrated OneDrive Files-On-Demand placeholder) is KEPT, not tombstoned fleet-wide. Plus enumerateConfig now LOGS a directory-list failure instead of silently treating the dir as empty. Correct-by-construction (owner declined a bulk guard, wanted proper behavior). Fail-first regression in reconcile.test ('CONFIRMED absence'): a placeholder file is not tombstoned; a genuinely-deleted file still is. Resolves issueFalseAbsenceDelete.
        action configListSetMerge; // Config-sync hardening (issueConfigListDisable) + real-Obsidian config-sync coverage. #1: community-plugins.json is now UNION-merged as a grow-only set of enabled ids (configsync.ts isEnabledListConfig/mergeEnabledPluginsJson + a reconcileOne branch), so a shorter synced copy can never DISABLE a locally-installed plugin (nor drop SelfSync's own id); enables propagate, disables don't (correct-by-construction, not a guard). #2: a two-device real-Obsidian e2e (client/e2e-obsidian/configsync.pwspec.ts) proves config sync propagates a plugin A→B and B's own enabled plugin survives A's shorter list. Verified: configsync.test set-merge units, reconcile.test union-merge integration (fail-first), full headless suite 396 passed, and the Playwright+CDP config-sync test green. Resolves issueConfigListDisable.
        action deliverableTestGate; // STANDING GATE (D0026): "all deliverable tests green + coverage floors met" as a COMPUTED, reverifiable fact. method=test DoD names the reproducible gate (reverify.toml + CI); its TestResult is the immutable point-in-time observation. Mapped in deliverable-manifest.txt to server/src + client/src + the test trees, so ANY source change makes it suspect (keel suspect) and `keel reverify` re-runs the gate + re-stamps at HEAD — never a prose pass-attestation.

        // ---- outstanding (open frontier) ----
        action b7AuthHardening;     // B7: expiring/revocable tokens, token-only persist, TLS guidance, optional E2EE
        action b9DurabilityStreaming; // B9 Part A: append-only index journal (D0010)
        action streamingReassembly; // B9 Part B: streamed reassembly of large downloads (desktop streams, mobile buffers)
        action b11ParallelChunk;    // B11: parallelize chunk transfer (large-file perf)
        action l3GuiPass;           // L3: manual Obsidian GUI verification of 0.6.0 (esp. switch + indicators)
        action l4MobileOndevice;    // L4: on-device mobile run (foreground sync, resumable initial sync)
        action vaultSharingP1;      // vault sharing Phase 1: server ACL + authz + registration policy + web admin
        action shareClientConsume;  // vault sharing Phase 2: plugin syncs vaults shared with you
        action configSyncSafety;    // 0.10.4: config sync additive + adjudicated (never delete/resurrect); crash fix
        action requirementTraceabilityBackfill; // CR d0011: backfill the missing SR->Test #Verify traceability (resolves the escape Issue)
        action settingsGroupingPolish; // DONE (inspect, 26dc385): the settings tab is grouped into a status-first card + four concern sections (Setup & transitions / Connection / What syncs / Advanced), each a headed group of named+described Settings — never atomized-per-setting. The intelligent grouping was built into the goal-#1 config-UX overhaul (informed by LiveSync's confusing-settings study), so the end-of-project polish pass confirms it reads sensibly with no rework needed. Resolves issueSettingsGrouping.
        action critiqueClientWave;      // DONE (0.10.14): the 5 client data-integrity/correctness fixes from the adversarial critique
        action critiqueServerHardening; // DONE (0.10.16, code): SEC-1/2/MED-1/MED-2/MED-3(semaphore)/DI-3/DI-4/SEC-3 + the Low backlog — cargo-green, needs operator redeploy
        action round1CriticFixes;       // DONE (0.10.17): 15 of 18 fresh Round-1 3-lens critic findings fixed (6 SEC, 4 DI, 5 CONC); 3 dispositioned accept-risk/defer
        action round1DeferredHardening;  // DONE (0.10.32, 7524aba): the 3 deferred Round-1 findings — SEC#4 runtime orphan-chunk GC (ContentStore::sweep_orphans, upload-driven + interval-gated + TTL-spared), CONC#5 durable pending-switch (clear only after switchTo succeeds), and DI#4 (reindex prefer-store-over-stale-mirror, already shipped by round6CriticFixes 0.10.27). Resolves issueOrphanChunkQuota + issueSwitchPendingClear.
        action residualLowFindings;      // DONE (backlog sprint 2): both platform/effort-deferred LOW findings are now fixed, the capabilities they waited on having since landed. issueStreamWholeHash — the client's incremental SHA-256 (streamhash.ts Sha256, R17) EXISTS and streamFileToDisk uses it (sync.ts:121-130 verifies the reassembled whole-file hash before the atomic rename) → resolved (was stale-open). issueReindexSingleChunk — a Rust CDC chunker (server/src/chunker.rs) now matches the client gear-hash BYTE-FOR-BYTE (golden-vector parity test both sides), and reindex chunks each file with it instead of one giant blob. Tests: chunker::matches_the_client_chunker_byte_for_byte, vault::reindex_chunks_a_large_file_into_many_chunks_that_reassemble, client chunker-parity. (The two ACCEPTED-inherent/cosmetic siblings — issuePullTOCTOUResidual, issueTransientGreenLight — remain signed off won't-fix under D0020.)
        action cmmcComplianceBacklog;    // MOOTED by D0027 (2026-07-15): its sole scope was the two CUI-DATA-specific controls — SC.3.13.11 (FIPS crypto) + SC.3.13.16 (CUI-at-rest). The owner confirmed this deployment stores NO CUI, so both are formally NOT APPLICABLE (recorded as D0027, which now #Resolves issueCmmcFips + issueCmmcAtRest as a mooting Decision). No code items remain. Service-protecting controls (auth/MFA/lockout, TLS SC.3.13.8, access control, audit) stay in force. Reopens only if a deployment ever stores CUI.
        action cmmcForcedChangeReuse;    // DONE (server, real-tested): password-reuse history (IA.3.5.8 — users.rs is_password_reused/rotate_password, cap 5) + forced-change-on-reset/create (IA.3.5.9 — must_change flag enforced in the AuthToken extractor; blocks all routes but change/logout). Tests: users.rs reuse_history + must_change_flag; admin.rs password_change_rejects_reuse + admin_created_account_is_forced_to_change_password. Resolves issueCmmcPwReuse + issueCmmcForcedChange.
        action cmmcMfa;                  // DONE (server, real-tested): multifactor authentication (IA.3.5.3 — TOTP RFC 6238 second factor + single-use recovery codes for privileged/admin accounts, self-enrolled via /admin, verified at login). Self-contained crypto (totp.rs, no new deps) pinned to RFC 4231/6238 vectors. Tests: totp.rs totp_rfc6238_vectors + hmac_sha1_rfc4231; admin.rs mfa_totp_full_lifecycle. Resolves issueCmmcMfa.
        action critRoundCmmc;            // DONE (server + client, real-tested): white-glove CMMC L2 / NIST 800-171 rev2 assessor round (AC/IA/AU + SC/SI/CM). Headline: fixed an OVERSTATED-MET — IA.3.5.3 MFA was opt-in only, not required for privileged accounts; added REQUIRE_ADMIN_MFA=1 enforcement in require_admin (an admin can't act until TOTP-enrolled) + honest posture. Also: audit failed MFA enable/disable (AU.3.3.1); per-user WS connection sub-cap (SC.3.13.1, no single-account notification DoS); centralized the client cleartext-http refusal in httpReq so ALL token-bearing account calls refuse http-to-remote (SC.3.13.8 now genuinely whole-channel → met); broadened the boot guard to the whole weak/short bootstrap-password class (CM.3.4.2). Honesty reclassifications: 3.13.8 partial→met, 3.1.11 met→partial (idle = liveness + absolute cap, not user-inactivity). Tests: admin.rs require_admin_mfa_blocks_admin_until_totp_enrolled; config.rs refuses_known_weak_and_short; transport.test SC.3.13.8. Resolves issueCmmc2Mfa/AuditMfa/WsPerUser/Cleartext/BootGuard.
        action critRoundStd;             // DONE (client + server, real-tested): standard 3-lens critique round (data-integrity + security + sync). Fixed 6: reconcileDelta now supplies locallyPresent so the C1 transient-unreadable guard is active on the poll-delta path (KEYSTONE — a present-but-unreadable file during a delta could silently resurrect a deletion or lose a diverged edit; found INDEPENDENTLY by two critics); delete-local restore is CAS-guarded (expectedVersion 0, no lost update); a download vault-switch applies the bulk-delete ratio guard (a partial "ready" manifest can't mass-delete local-only notes); realtimeConnected reset on connect (no stale-green flash); server commit routes LARGE reassemblies through a permit pool (bounds aggregate memory-amplification DoS across many vaults); the WS path now enforces the must_change gate. Tests: reconcile.test crit-round cases; server suite green. Resolves issueCritDeltaGuard/RestoreCas/DownloadSwitch/RealtimeStale/CommitDoS/WsMustChange.
        action hfConfirmAndSidePicking;  // DONE (1.5.2, client-only): HF fixes — in-app confirm modal + side-picking consistency (PATCH). A small in-app ConfirmModal (confirm.ts) replaces all four native window.confirm() destructive guards (mirror-switch/fork-overwrite/leave-share/sign-out), consistent + styleable on mobile. Standardized the 'pick a side' surfaces: removed the biasing CTA from the unbiased note-conflict + config-conflict choices (a highlighted default on a 50/50 irreversible choice invited a capture-error tap); aligned config vocabulary to 'Use this device's' / 'Use the synced version'; CTA reserved for the genuinely-safe default (vault-switch Merge). Resolves issueSidePickingInconsistent/issueNativeConfirmMobile.
        action hfStatusSurfacingAndPreview;  // DONE (1.6.0, client-only, FEATURE): final human-factors batch — surface status where it's reachable, set expectations before a config commit, keep long-op state visible. (1) A 'Sync status' command toasts the current status words on demand — a one-tap readout on mobile, where the only persistent indicator is a textless sidebar icon (a truly persistent on-screen TEXT indicator isn't available: Obsidian mobile has no status bar and view.addAction is icon-only — honest partial mitigation of issueMobileStatusTextless). (2) ConfigDirectionModal intro copy now sets expectations before a whole-side overwrite — 'only files that differ change, everything else is left alone, later edits reconcile normally' (a true diff/count preview needs a local-vs-server compare the modal lacks; deferred — issueBlindConfigOverwrite copy-level mitigation). (3) statusDisplay shows a persistent 'Switching vault…' state whenever a fork/switch is in flight, DERIVED from the saved pendingSwitch flag so it survives suspend/resume and clears when the switch reconcile completes (issueLongOpTransientCompletion). MINOR per semver (adds the status command + persistent switch state). Resolves issueMobileStatusTextless/issueBlindConfigOverwrite/issueLongOpTransientCompletion.
        action hfStatusAndWarnings;  // DONE (1.5.1, client-only): human-factors fixes — status correctness + warning calibration (PATCH). statusDisplay idle on a READ-ONLY vault now reads 'Synced (read-only) — your edits stay on this device' with a lock glyph (was a misleading green 'Fully synced'); idle uses a STEADY glyph (check/lock) instead of the spinner, so a healthy polling device isn't stuck at a permanent yellow spinner (the spinner is reserved for connecting/syncing); the vault-switch download confirm now says local removals go to the recoverable vault trash (was the miscalibrated 'can't be undone'), reserving heavier wording for the server-upload case. Resolves issueStatusIndicatorMisleads/issueMiscalibratedSwitchWarning.
        action deferUxEnhancements;  // DECLINED (2026-07-13, human-attested): three UX-critique findings the user chose NOT to act on now — the obsidian:// protocol handler (issueNoProtocolHandler), setup-wizard state persistence (issueWizardStatePersistence), and the deeper IA restructures + residual lows (issueDeepIaRestructure). Real but larger; deferred by explicit wweatherholtz instruction ("record these as declined items"). This action IS the recorded deferral disposition (no code); resolves those three issues so they're tracked-as-declined rather than dangling.
        action surfaceSharingAndConflicts;  // DONE (1.5.0, client-only, FEATURE): surfaced the inbound-sharing + conflict flows the critique found undiscoverable. New command-palette commands: 'Switch vault' (was only in settings), 'Redeem a share link', 'Resolve conflicts' (routes to whichever kind is pending, else a notice); the setup command renamed 'Set up / reconfigure connection'. A 'Redeem a share link' button added to the UNCONFIGURED status card (the new-recipient entry point — no longer requires knowing to paste a share link into a setup field). And startRedeem now OPENS the Switch modal after an already-signed-in redeem (redeemed vault appears in 'Shared with you') instead of leaving the second step to a missable toast. MINOR per semver. Resolves issueSharingConflictsDiscoverability.
        action pluginAdoptionRestartHint;  // DONE (1.4.0, client-only, FEATURE): closes the plugin-adoption ending — after 'Install all from the sync' the plugins looked synced but weren't active (Obsidian loads plugins only at startup; the only hint was a transient toast). Now a STANDING mod-warning banner in the Synced-community-plugins group counts plugins adopted-but-not-installed-locally and says 'fully close and reopen Obsidian (on mobile, swipe the app away) to enable them'; plus a 'Checking the server for plugins…' placeholder while the server list hasn't populated yet (so a fresh vault doesn't read as 'nothing to sync'). MINOR per semver (new user-facing state). Resolves issuePluginAdoptionSilentRestart.
        action guardDestructiveActions;  // DONE (1.3.2, client-only): UX-critique data-safety guards (PATCH). The vault-switch Download/Upload MIRROR modes now confirm() before deleting local-only / remote-only files (naming which side loses files, 'can't be undone') — previously a single tap; Fork refuses/confirms when the name matches an existing owned vault (it uploads unconditionally, so a collision would overwrite); Sign out confirm()s (token-only mode has no saved password → re-login needed). Merge (safe default) still needs no confirm. Resolves issueUnguardedDestructiveActions.
        action uxPolishBundle;  // DONE (1.3.1, client-only): UX-critique quick-win polish (all fixes/copy → PATCH). Recovery error messages now name real buttons ('Reconfigure'/'Switch') not the command-palette name; setup/consent banner renders line breaks (white-space:pre-wrap); Max file size validates on blur (notice + revert, no silent fail); conflict-log breadcrumb → 'Settings → Conflicts'; 3 log-viewer toasts gained the 'SelfSync:' prefix; 'Keep the other device's'; 'fully close and reopen Obsidian' (mobile-clear) replaces 'reload Obsidian'; change-password warns other token-only devices need the new password; removed dead statusTitle() (+ its test) that had diverged from statusDisplay(). Resolves issueUxQuickWins.
        action forkVault;  // DONE (1.3.0, client-only, FEATURE): a direct "Fork this vault" action (Switch modal) — copies the CURRENT vault's local content into a NEW vault you own and switches this device to it; the original is untouched. Especially useful on a read-only shared vault (yields your own editable copy). Reuses tested primitives: createRemoteVault(name) then switchToVault(name,'upload','',false). Makes explicit what was previously a manual switch-to-new-vault + upload. MINOR per semver.
        action statusDetailAndResuming;  // DONE (1.2.0, client-only, FEATURE): the status line was a bare "Syncing…" with no detail, so when nothing was pending it looked like nothing was happening. Now statusDisplay(phase) always says WHAT: "Syncing… N pending" while transferring, "Syncing… checking for changes" while assessing (never a bare label); idle distinguishes "Fully synced" vs "Synced (polling)" by realtime health. Plus a new transient "Resuming…" state shown after a context switch (mobile resume via visibilitychange) while sync state is re-assessed — set in onResume, cleared once the phase settles (idle/offline) or transfers start (pending>0). One source of truth used by the settings row + ribbon/status-bar tooltip. MINOR per semver (new user-facing state).
        action adoptServerPlugins;  // DONE (1.1.0, client-only, FEATURE, extends D0025): fixes the fresh-vault bootstrap gap — the plugin allowlist was built from LOCALLY-INSTALLED plugins only, so a new vault (none of the source vault's plugins installed) had an empty list and could never adopt them, and expecting the user to pre-install what they don't yet know exists is backwards. Now reconcileAll reports the server's community-plugin ids (onRemotePlugins); settings shows the UNION of installed + server-side plugins (server-only ones labelled "from the sync — will be installed"), ticking one pulls its files = installs it (download-only for not-installed); plus a one-click "Install all from the sync" bootstrap. Respects the peer-plugin-code gate; opt-in (running third-party code stays a deliberate act). MINOR bump per semver (new capability, not a fix).
        action pendingExcludesDeclined;  // DONE (1.0.39, client-only): FIELD — reopening a vault showed 20+ pending syncs that never transferred. The pending pre-classifier counted remote files this device DECLINES (config surface off / plugin not allowlisted) — reconcileOne skips them, so the count never drained (worse on mobile, which backgrounds mid-pass). Fix: reconcileAll + reconcileDelta exclude accepts()-filtered files from the pending set (honest 'work this device will do'), and surface them via a new onDeclined callback → a coalesced, change-only log naming the community plugins / config files on the server that aren't in this device's selection + how to enable them (also explains that plugin sync is opt-in on BOTH ends). Resolves issuePendingCountsDeclinedFiles.
        action configSyncPerPluginDirection;  // DONE (1.0.38, client-only, extends D0025): per-plugin first-contact direction — the "lighter form" the user asked for. Each synced community plugin carries its own direction (configSync.pluginDir, persisted, keyed by id), shown as an inline download/upload dropdown that appears only when the plugin is synced (read-only → "download only" text). Defaults to the Community surface's direction. The synced-plugins list is now COLLAPSIBLE (<details>, expanded when ≤8, state persists across re-renders) so a big roster doesn't flood the pane, independent of a mixed per-plugin direction set. main.ts setPluginSync/setPluginDir/communityConfigDir; recordConfigConflict prefers a plugin path's own pluginDir over the surface direction; loadSettings keeps a fresh pluginDir. Read-only forces download everywhere.
        action configSyncFirstContactDirection;  // DONE (1.0.37, client-only, implements D0025): settings (config) sync now declares an EXPLICIT first-contact direction PER SURFACE when turned on — {download = adopt synced, upload = make this device's canonical}, MERGE dropped (config is opaque, a line-merge could corrupt it). Replaces the reactive per-file 'keep local / take remote' prompt-on-divergence with an upfront intent (ConfigDirectionModal). Read-only shares: offered, default OFF, download-only (opt-in; never pushes; never auto-clobbers the reader's config). Mechanism: session-transient per-surface pendingConfigDir consumed by recordConfigConflict to auto-resolve a NO-BASE divergence via resolveConfigConflict; a later concurrent edit (shared base) still prompts. Pure configSurfaceOf + configAutoResolveChoice. Accepted by wweatherholtz (per-surface + read-only-default-off).
        action configSyncEventDriven;  // DONE (1.0.36, client-only): made mobile config DETECTION event-driven (user direction). The WS already makes the RECEIVE path event-driven (server poke → pull); the gap was the SENDER noticing its OWN config edit, where mobile lacks a reliable `raw` FS event. Now Obsidian UI events are proxies: css-change (theme/snippet/appearance) + layout-change (plugin toggle / panes) TRIGGER the cheap stat-skipping config scan on demand (coalesced + rate-limited to ~once/CONFIG_EVENT_MIN_GAP_MS, since layout-change also fires on plain navigation). The 30s periodic scan is demoted to a BACKSTOP for the rare change that fires no event. Common mobile config edits now sync near-instantly instead of ≤30s. Follows the 1.0.35 cheap-scan (fastCheapConfigScan) which made frequent scanning viable.
        action fastCheapConfigScan;  // DONE (1.0.35, client-only): FIELD — config sync felt ~5 min on mobile. Desktop is live (vault `raw` event); mobile lacks it and fell back to a 120s config re-hash + suspends when backgrounded. Fix (user chose 'cheap fast scan'): (1) reconcileLocalConfig skips a file whose on-disk (size,mtime) match the base stat-stamp → the scan runs often without re-hashing every synced plugin's bytes; (2) CONFIG_SCAN_INTERVAL_MS 120s→30s; (3) a visibilitychange listener forces a config scan on app-resume. Detection ~2 min → ~30s (instant on reopen). Resolves issueConfigSyncMobileLatency.
        action editorStatusCleanupOnUnload;  // DONE (1.0.34, client-only): FIELD — the note header stacked 6 sync icons (1 green + 5 red). The opt-in in-editor indicator is added via view.addAction, which Obsidian does NOT auto-clean on unload (unlike addRibbonIcon/addStatusBarItem), and onunload didn't remove it — so every plugin update orphaned the old instance's icon and the new instance added another (dead ones frozen at their last phase). Fix: onunload now removes all editorActionEls (mirrors the setEditorStatus-off cleanup) → idempotent across reloads. Existing orphans clear on one Obsidian restart. Resolves issueEditorStatusIconLeakOnReload.
        action connErrorAbortsPass;  // DONE (1.0.33, client-only): FIELD — a mobile resume before DNS was ready flooded the log with ~200 per-file UnknownHostException errors (a whole-connection failure isolated per-file, meant for one bad file). New isConnectionError classifier (host-resolution + connection-refused/reset/unreachable; deliberately NOT per-file content/read errors) makes reconcileAll/reconcileDelta/config loops ABORT the pass on the first connection error (shared connAbort flag short-circuits the remaining files) → engine goes offline + backs off ONCE. A genuine single-file error still isolates. Resolves issueConnErrorPerFileFlood.
        action conflictReadOnlyAndBinaryCorrectness;  // DONE (1.0.31, client-only): 3-lens critique + field-report fixes to conflict/sync correctness. (1) FIELD: read-only vault no longer manufactures unsyncable, permanently-flagged conflict copies for a no-base divergence — on read-only, a copy is preserved ONLY for a genuine both-sides edit vs a known base (action 'merge'); a no-base divergence adopts the owner's bytes with NO copy; an existing conflict-copy file is no longer reported 'won't sync'. (2) F1 (High): the cosmetic-EOL guard + modal auto-dismiss are gated on isMergeable (extension + fatal-UTF-8), so a binary attachment can't be lossy-collapsed to 'equal' and silently clobbered. (3) F3: resolveNoteConflict 'keep mine' re-checks the stale-preview guard immediately before the write (TOCTOU). (4) F4: startPolling early-returns when unloading (no leaked interval on unload-during-connect). (5) F5: listNoteConflicts requires the original to exist (no look-alike/orphan flagged). (6) F6: resolveShareGrant fails closed on an unknown perm. Resolves issueFalseConflictReadOnlyBinary/issueCosmeticGuardBinaryClobber/issueResolveMineToctou/issueUnloadPollLeak/issueConflictCopyLookalikeDelete/issueShareGrantFailOpen.
        action shareRedeemStoreConsistency;  // DONE (server): 3-lens critique fixes to share-redeem cross-store consistency. (1) F2a: shares.rs grant() snapshots + restores its grant set on a save() I/O failure, so a failed grant never lingers in memory (the redeem rollback can't leave a live grant + a re-redeemable link). (2) F2b: share-link self-redeem (owner redeems own link) now unredeems (releases the claim) so it doesn't burn the single-use invite. Resolves issueGrantSaveRollback/issueSelfRedeemBurnsLink.
        action shareLinkRedeemConsumeLast;  // DONE (1.0.30 server): server dual-source sweep (client-audit follow-up) finding. share_link_redeem consumed the single-use link (.share-links.json) BEFORE the grant (.shares.json) succeeded, so a recoverable grant failure (owner at cap / grant I/O error) — or a crash between the two file writes — permanently BURNED the invite with no grant. Fix: redeem still claims the link atomically (single-use preserved under concurrency), but the handler now rolls the claim back via ShareLinkStore::unredeem on BOTH failure branches → the link survives to retry (only the narrow crash-between-writes window remains, accepted). Fails closed (redeemed_by never feeds authz). Resolves issueShareLinkBurnedOnFailedGrant.
        action shareRefreshedOnConnect;  // DONE (1.0.30, client-only): killed a second dual-source-of-truth (client-side audit follow-up to D0024). The cached vaultOwner/vaultReadOnly were frozen at redeem time and drifted from the server's share grant (the authority) — an owner flipping read↔write or revoking access was invisible until a manual re-Switch. Fix: connect() now re-derives our access from listShared() on EVERY reconnect via the pure resolveShareGrant(grants, owner, vault) → the cached flag is a projection of the grant, not a copy. Revocation is caught before a push would 403 (clear card message, files untouched, auto-recovers if re-granted). Own vaults short-circuit (no extra call). Tests: sharelink.test resolveShareGrant (notShared / read→read-only / readWrite-upgrade / revoked-when-absent).
        action conflictModelDerivedFromVault;  // DONE (1.0.29, client-only, implements D0024): re-architected conflict tracking to kill the dual-source-of-truth. NOTE conflicts are now DERIVED PURELY FROM THE VAULT (deriveNoteConflicts over the vault file list; the strict-named copy file IS the record) — settings.noteConflicts array + recordNoteConflict/clearNoteConflict deleted; listNoteConflicts/count/badge/modal are pure projections; resolveNoteConflict is total/idempotent (missing copy → no-op, no 'File does not exist'). CONFIG conflicts stay the reconcile-refreshed store (no artifact by design). Fixes stale entries, dual-truth counts, blank modal — by construction, not patching.
        action pendingProgressAndConflictResilience;  // DONE (1.0.28, client-only): (1) sync progress reworked from 'N/M files examined' (total is noise) to '# PENDING' — files that actually need transfer, driving to 0. reconcileAll pre-classifies pending cheaply from remote-hash-vs-base + real tombstones + new-local (no local hashing); reconcileDelta's changed set IS the pending set. onProgress is now single-arg (pending). (2) Conflict-modal RESILIENCE: a stale conflict entry (copy/note already gone → 'File does not exist') no longer aborts the whole modal ('Couldn't load conflicts') — each auto-dismiss entry is isolated in its own try/catch and skipped.
        action conflictModalFixAndSyncProgress;  // DONE (1.0.27, client-only): (1) the 'Resolve conflicts' modal rendered BLANK — the auto-dismiss loop awaited through all N files before drawing, and an error left it empty. Fixed: run() shows an immediate 'Checking conflicts…' placeholder, auto-dismisses cosmetic copies WITH a visible progress count, then draws; wrapped in try/catch so an error shows a message, never a blank body. (2) Sync PROGRESS: reconcileAll fires onProgress(done,total); the plugin throttles to integer-% and surfaces 'Syncing… N/M' in the status-card row + the light tooltip (syncstate light('syncing', detail)).
        action falseEolConflictFixAndDiff;  // DONE (1.0.26, client-only): sync falsely flagged 46 'conflicts' whose two versions were identical — they differed ONLY by line endings (Windows CRLF desktop vs mobile LF) and, with no common base (first sync/adopt of two independent-but-identical copies), decide() returned conflict-copy and spawned a spurious copy per file. Fix: sameIgnoringEol() guard in reconcileOne's merge/conflict-copy branch converges on the remote bytes (records base, NO copy) when the only difference is EOL/trailing-newline. UX: NoteConflictModal now (a) auto-dismisses cosmetic-only copies already on disk (clears the 46 without 46 clicks) and (b) shows a real line-level DIFF (unifiedLineDiff via merge.lcsPairs; −other/+this-device, context dimmed) for genuine conflicts — the requested diff view.
        action granteeLeaveShare;        // DONE (1.0.25, server+client): a shared-with user can now DECLINE/LEAVE a shared vault (drop their OWN access) — previously only the owner could revoke. SERVER: DELETE /api/shared {owner,vault} (api::leave_share) forces grantee=caller so you can only remove your own grant; audited. CLIENT: transport.leaveShare + plugin.leaveSharedVault (also disconnects if it's the vault you're currently syncing; local files kept) + a 'Leave' button per entry in the Switch modal's 'Shared with you' list (confirm dialog). e2e proves 200-before / 403-after / gone-from-shared-list against the real server.
        action settingsPanelTargetedCleanup;  // DONE (1.0.24, client-only): targeted settings-panel declutter (user-approved scope). 'Redeem link' removed from the current-vault row (it gains access to a DIFFERENT vault, not an action on the current one) and moved into the Switch-vault modal as 'Redeem a share link' — it belongs with choosing/gaining vaults (redeeming adds to 'Shared with you'). 'Reconfigure' (was on the Server row) and 'Disconnect' (was in the status row, duplicating 'Sign out') moved to Advanced → Connection with a description distinguishing Reconfigure / Disconnect / Sign out. Status card is now leaner (Server fact has no button; Vault row: Share [if owned] + Switch; status row: Diagnose + Add a device). Answered separately: the shared 'default' vault was created by the pre-1.0.19 multi-vault modal (audit log share_link_create target will/default) — clutter now removed.
        action redeemE2ECoverage;        // DONE (test-only): the missing end-to-end test that would have caught the 1.0.20-1.0.23 share-flow gaps in ONE run instead of four user-found regressions. sharing-e2e.spec adds 'must-change account → change password → redeem a share LINK → sync' against the REAL server: asserts a fresh admin-created account is must-change-gated (login ok + /api/vaults 403), changePassword clears it (200), a read-write share LINK is created + redeemed (binds the grant, single-use), and the recipient syncs the owner-qualified vault. NodeTransport gained loginFull/createUserRaw/changePassword/createShareLink/redeemShareLink/listShared/rawStatus. Root-caused the blind spot: the createUser helper HID must-change (did the forced change internally), so no test ever drove a must-change account through login/redeem.
        action wizardForcedPasswordChange;  // DONE (1.0.23, client-only): a fresh/admin-created account hit 'vaults: HTTP 403' when signing in via the setup wizard (incl. the guided-redeem flow). Cause: the account is must-change-password gated (IA.3.5.9 — every route 403s until the password is set), but the wizard ignored the flag and barreled into listVaults. Fix: HttpTransport.login now returns {token, mustChange}; the wizard, on mustChange, shows a 'Set a new password' step (changePassword → fresh un-gated token) then continues (afterAuthenticated: redeem in redeem-mode, else load vaults). loginRemote (established re-login) unwraps .token.
        action guidedRedeemViaSetup;     // DONE (1.0.22, client-only): a share link now BOOTSTRAPS setup instead of requiring you to be set up first (the anti-pattern the user flagged — the link IS the onboarding). plugin.startRedeem(link) is the single entry: if already signed in to the link's server, redeem now (+ 'use Switch'); otherwise open SetupWizardModal in REDEEM mode — server prefilled from the link, guide sign-in (login OR register), then finishRedeem() persists the session, redeems, adopts the shared vault (vaultId/vaultOwner/readOnly) and reconnects. No vault-picker step in redeem mode. The wizard's paste hand-off + Settings 'Redeem link' both route through this.
        action redeemNotSetUpGuardAndDirect;  // DONE (1.0.21, client-only): the 'Invalid URL' on redeem persisted after 1.0.20 because a SECOND new URL threw — redeemShareLink compared normalizeServer(this.settings.serverUrl) with an EMPTY serverUrl on a not-set-up device (new URL('') → 'Invalid URL'). Extracted redeemTargetError(linkServer, deviceServer): guards the empty/not-set-up case with clear guidance ('Set up SelfSync and sign in to <server> first') and the wrong-server case, no crash. Also: the setup-link paste hand-off now REDEEMS DIRECTLY (Notice on result) instead of opening the redeem modal — no second click. Redeem stays authenticated + server-specific (a fresh device must sign in to the link's server first).
        action shareLinkUrlParseFix;     // DONE (1.0.20, client-only): redeeming a share link threw 'Failed to construct URL: Invalid URL' on Obsidian mobile. Root cause: parseShareLink/parseSetupLink did `new URL(link.replace(scheme,'https://'))` → `https://redeem?…`, a bare-label host the Android WebView URL parser rejects. Both now read the query DIRECTLY via URLSearchParams on the substring after '?' (no fake-host URL, decoding preserved). Regression test with the exact failing percent-encoded link.
        action shareCurrentVaultOnly;    // DONE (1.0.19, client-only): ShareManageModal simplified to share ONLY the vault this device is currently syncing (settings.vaultId) — no per-vault loop, no vault picker, no vault labels/headings (title 'Share this vault'). Drops the confusing multi-section modal (one block per owned vault, incl. the stray auto-created 'default') that made it easy to create a link for the wrong vault. A vault shared-with-you (vaultOwner set) or not-yet-synced shows a clear can't-share message. Pending links filtered to the current vault.
        action shareUxAndCaseInsensitiveNames;  // DONE (1.0.18): field-reported sharing/UX fixes. (1) Share/redeem errors surfaced 'is not valid JSON' — RequestUrlResponse.json throws on a plain-text error body; transport now reads r.text (errText helper) so the server's real message shows (share/unshare/create-link/redeem/create-vault). (2) Pasting a selfsync-share:// link into the device-setup 'Paste setup link' field failed 'Not a SelfSync setup link' — the paster now detects a share link (isShareLink) and hands off to RedeemShareLinkModal (prefilled). (3) Usernames are now CASE-INSENSITIVE (canonicalized to lowercase at login/register/users_create/share-grantee) — 'Will'/'DANA'/'Bhu' map to the one lowercase account; non-breaking since stored keys were always lowercase. Also explains the per-vault share sections (one per owned vault; the stray 'default' vault is the bootstrap auto-create).
        action usernameRuleAndUx;        // DONE (server-only): admin add-user rejected emails without stating why. safe_name now also admits '+' and '@' (path- + filesystem-safe, no traversal — enables email/plus-addressed usernames; still lowercase-canonical), a shared NAME_RULE string is surfaced in the 'invalid username' error (users_create + register), and admin_ui.html states the rule under the add-user row. Fixes the field report: silent-ish rejection with no expectation.
        action skipOsJunkFiles;          // DONE (1.0.17, client-only): the plugin now skips OS/tool junk (Thumbs.db, .DS_Store, desktop.ini, .git anywhere in the path, + .selfsync-part/.selfsync-tmp temps) instead of attempting to sync them and logging one HTTP 400 per file. isJunkFile() in configsync.ts is an EXACT mirror of the server's is_junk; folded into shouldSync (the shared io+reconcile accept gate) so junk is never pushed and no base is recorded (no phantom delete). Fixes the field-reported Thumbs.db 400 noise.
        action vaultNameAndSizeLimits;   // DONE (1.0.16, real-tested): two field-reported UX fixes. (1) VAULT NAME: the wizard + vault switcher now sanitizeVaultName() (trim + lowercase, matching the server's lowercase-only safe_name) before create, so "Testbrsin" becomes "testbrsin" instead of a bare HTTP 400; isValidVaultName tightened to lowercase-only (client rule == server rule) + a clear inline message. (2) CONFIGURABLE SIZE LIMITS: per-file cap was hard-coded (50 MB mobile / 200 MB desktop) — now a per-device "Max file size to sync (MB)" setting (default 200, maxSyncBytes()) and a server MAX_FILE_MB env (Config::max_file_bytes, default 512, enforced in api::commit; vault backstop raised to 4 GiB absolute). Answers the field reports: the mobile 50 MB skip + the vault-name 400.
        action deployComposeHardening;   // DONE: deploy/ compose cleanup + published server image. Removed the local `build: ../server` (the server now ships as a prebuilt GHCR image ghcr.io/williamweatherholtz/obsidian-selfsync-server, published by a new release.yml server-image job on each version tag; compose uses `image:`). Dropped redundant env (DATA_ROOT + BIND_ADDR — image-fixed internal address/path, not user knobs) and the no-op `expose:` (Compose same-network reachability needs neither expose nor ports). Added an explicit healthcheck (curl /health on the sync port, served on every surface) + Caddy `depends_on: service_healthy`. New deploy/docker-compose.noproxy.yml (server only, sync bound to 127.0.0.1:8080) for operators who terminate TLS themselves. Documented the REGISTRATION first-run-seed semantics (env seeds .registration.json only on first boot; afterward /admin is authoritative + persists across reboots — answers the reboot/override question honestly). doc-sync: deployment.md + README corrected (the stale `expose:`-not-`ports:` claim, env table, noproxy + image/pull guidance).
        action perfHarnessScaleLatency;  // DONE: headless real-world PERFORMANCE harness (client/perf, `npm run test:perf`) — spawns the real server + headless clients through the real chunk/reconcile engine, measuring SCALE (initial push/pull + no-op rescan by vault size) and PROPAGATION LATENCY (single-edit A->B round-trip). Results + interpretation in docs/architecture/92-perf-scale-latency.md: propagation is flat ~20-29ms p50 from 50->3000 notes (O(change)); no-op rescan sub-second at 3000 files (scan-skip); initial push is per-file-round-trip bound (~110 notes/s, debug/loopback floor). Env: loopback + debug build (a pessimistic floor).
        action perfDevicePass;           // OPEN: the real-device fidelity pass (desktop + phone via BRAT 1.0.15, real server/TLS/network) for scale + propagation — protocol + results template in docs/architecture/93-real-device-perf-protocol.md. Awaits the operator's hardware run; findings route as Issues.
        action capabilityShareLinks;     // DONE (server + client, real-tested): D0023 — share a vault by sending a single-use LINK (no username, in-plugin, no admin), redeem-binds-to-account. Server: sharelinks.rs store (.share-links.json, hashed/single-use/TTL'd, permission server-side) + owner-scoped create/list/revoke + AuthToken-gated redeem (mints a D0008 grant bound to the redeemer). Client: selfsync-share:// codec, transport methods, ShareManageModal create/pending-list/revoke + RedeemShareLinkModal + a settings "Redeem link" action. Implements D0023 / serves nVaultSharing. Tests: sharelinks.rs 3 unit + admin.rs 2 integration; client sharelink.test 6 + modals DOM 3.
        action acceptOpenEnumRisk;       // DONE (accept-risk, human-attested): open-registration username enumeration is accepted as inherent to open self-registration — de-oracling /api/register would break the UX (a user must be told a name is taken to pick another), and anyone can create accounts in that mode anyway. Mitigation is operator guidance: run registration invite-only/closed (the default), which removes the public register surface entirely. Resolves issueCritOpenEnum.
        action acceptMobileFsyncRisk;    // DONE (accept-risk, human-attested): the mobile buffered-write fsync durability gap is accepted as a known, intractable platform limitation — mobile exposes no fsync API, so the narrow crash-window (a pulled note lost between write and OS flush while base persisted) cannot be closed in code; desktop is durable. Resolves issueCritMobileFsync.
        action critResidual2;            // DONE (server + client, real-tested): two more residuals cleared. WS half-open liveness (SC-adjacent) — the server sends an application heartbeat every ~30s (ws.rs) and the client runs a liveness timer (main.ts) that treats the socket as dead + re-dials if no frame arrives within WS_STALE_MS, so the status light no longer stays green over a half-open socket (browsers hide protocol ping/pong from JS). Audit source-IP (AU.3.3.2) — require_admin now threads the caller's ClientIp, so the high-value privileged-function-denied events carry the source (read-only-route denials keep "-", proxy-correlated). Tests: syncstate.test isWsStale; server admin suite green with the require_admin signature change. Resolves issueCritWsLiveness + issueCmmc2AuditSource.
        action critResidualEasy;         // DONE (server, real-tested): the two low-effort residuals cleared — TOTP in-window replay protection (users.rs records the last consumed 30s step per user; a code from a consumed step is rejected, RFC 6238 §5.2) and the SC.3.13.13 claim-wording correction (sync allowlist, not an execution trust-prompt gate). Tests: totp_code_cannot_be_replayed_within_its_window. Resolves issueCritTotpReplay + issueCmmc2MobileCodeWording.
        action critRoundResidual;        // OPEN: accepted/deferred findings from the standard critique round — open-registration username enumeration (inherent UX-vs-enumeration tradeoff), TOTP in-window replay (standard RFC 6238 weakness; would need last-step tracking), WS half-open client liveness (needs app-level ping/pong — a protocol change), and mobile buffered-write fsync-durability (inherent to the mobile adapter's lack of an fsync API). Honestly open — planned/accepted, per the round notes.
        action uiFunctionalAudit;        // DONE (client + server, real-tested): end-to-end functional audit of BOTH UIs (admin web page + Obsidian plugin) — every interactive control traced to its behavior. Fixed 9 wiring defects across the three classes (discarded control effect, dual-truth/stale indicator, no-op/dead-end dialog): admin A1 sign-out revokes server session, A2 MFA-enable reflects enabled state, A3 forced-change login screen, A4 owner-vault sub-row reconciles after repair/delete, A5 no Repair on a "missing" vault; plugin P1 wizard honors token-only-at-rest, P2 config toggles apply immediately, P3 lastSyncedAt persisted, P4 status light reflects real WebSocket state. Guards: server admin.rs (must_change lifecycle, grant/revoke, delete, reindex/prune HTTP, invite list/delete); client syncstate.test (light realtime), wizardsteps.test (wizardCredentials token-only), plugin-wiring.test (applyConfigSyncChange kicks a scan); e2e-helpers fixed for the forced-change flow. Resolves issueUi*.
        action round2CriticFixes;        // DONE (0.10.18): 15 of 16 fresh Round-2 3-lens critic findings fixed (4 DI, 6 CONC, 4 SEC + 1 note); 1 accepted (residual pull TOCTOU, inherent)
        action round3CriticFixes;        // DONE (0.10.19): 6 of 8 fresh Round-3 3-lens critic findings fixed (1 DI, 3 CONC, 2 SEC); 2 deferred (streamed whole-file hash, reindex single-chunk)
        action round4CriticFixes;        // DONE (0.10.20): 2 of 2 fresh Round-4 findings fixed (1 DI MED, 1 CONC LOW); SECURITY LENS CONVERGED (0 findings); 1 cosmetic accepted
        action round5CriticFixes;        // DONE (0.10.21): 3 Round-5 final-adversary correctness fixes (Unicode case-collision, legacy-key delete, revoke-before-purge); holistic verdict = data-safety sound
        action round5CompletenessFollowups; // DONE (0.10.33, 10a7154): the holistic-round remainder — items 1/3/4 (version handshake, admin reindex, commit CAS) shipped earlier under preReleaseHardening; this closes item 7 (cosmetic conflict-copy: stream-fail orphan cleanup + live-hash tag), items 5/6 (persisted-data forward-migration seam client-side + SQLite schema_version tag server-side + lazy/runtime-GC requirement wording), and item 2 (orchestration test-harness: the raw-event config pipeline incl. the self-folder security filter now has a direct plugin-wiring test; SEC-3 no-auto-enable is round6, WS-revocation is server-side ACL). Resolves issueOrchestrationUntested + issueDataMigration + issueConflictCopyCosmetic.
        action pluginShareOptIn;          // DONE (0.10.23): community plugins are opt-in (allowlist), not default-share — a new install isn't auto-pushed; + bulk share-all/none
        action fsmRefactor;               // DONE (0.10.24): one authoritative operational FSM (SyncEngine: serial event queue) replaces the scattered flags + parallel recovery — the CONC-R* race class is now structurally impossible
        action deleteLocalTombstoneGate;  // DONE (0.10.25): CRITICAL data-loss fix — delete-local requires a real deletion tombstone, never mere absence; + plugin-wiring integration tests + e2e harness repair
        action preReleaseHardening;       // DONE (0.10.26): shippable round-5 completeness items + the 2 timing crutches — protocol version handshake, admin vault reindex, commit optimistic-concurrency (CAS); token-TTL crutch → optimistic+reactive-401; config-scan poll-count → wall-clock
        action round6CriticFixes;         // DONE (0.10.27): 3 High + 4 Med + 2 Low from the Round-6 3-lens critique — tombstone-cap removal (resurrection fix), CAS-409 event-path isolation, SEC-3 owner-direction RCE + CSS gate, single-flight re-login, failToOffline connected-drop, reindex collision-guard + prefer-store; 1 Low (share-create enumeration) accept-risk
        action round7RecoveryFixes;       // DONE (0.10.28): recovery-lens bugs — reindex recovers from the chunk store + admin force (RC-2, unbrick), 404 vault-gone message (RC-3), per-vault admin delete (RC-4)
        action sqliteMigration;           // DONE (05e655b; server-only, no plugin release): per-vault SQLite (WAL) index behind the SqliteIndex seam, replacing the JSON snapshot+journal — resolves the storage-format-dependent scale findings (RS-2/5/6/7) + hardens against index corruption (WAL + page checksums). JSON->SQLite data migration WAIVED by owner ('nuke away'); fresh start + reindex rebuilds from the chunk store + mirror. Postgres deferred behind the seam.
        action resourceScaleFixes;        // DONE (0.10.30): RS-1 (evict idle vault handles with no WS subscribers, bounding server RAM) + RS-4 (cap merge-ancestor base text at 1 MiB, bounding client RAM/data.json)
        action incrementalReconcile;      // DONE (0.10.29): RS-3 — a remote poke reconciles only the delta's changed paths (reconcileDelta), not a full-vault re-hash; the full reconcileAll is reserved for the config scan + version rewind
        action scaleHardening;            // DONE (05e655b): the umbrella for the Round-7 resource/scale findings, delivered by the three split actions — RS-1 handle eviction + RS-4 base-text cap (resourceScaleFixes, 0.10.30), RS-3 incremental reconcile (incrementalReconcile, 0.10.29), RS-2 per-write index clone / RS-5 version-indexed changes / RS-6 incremental snapshot / RS-7 bounded cold-open (sqliteMigration, the storage-engine decision D0018). Every RS-1..7 finding is now shipped or mooted.
        action historyRebase;             // DONE (0.10.31, 8c69b8b, D0019): the deletion-history HORIZON — the server tracks a history_floor (raised to the current version when a rebuild-from-disk reindex loses tombstones), exposed in changes; a below-floor client (floor advanced past its stored one, or a version rewind) stays conservative (keep + push, never delete without a tombstone) and surfaces ONE batched notice, fixing the corrupt-reindex resurrection (RC-1) without an arbitrary cap.
        action tombstonePrune;            // DONE (server, 8025fb2, D0019): the deliberate OPERATOR prune — SqliteIndex::prune_tombstones(floor) drops tombstones below the floor + raises history_floor to it (atomic); Vault::prune_history clamps floor to [current floor, version]; POST /api/admin/prune-history exposes it (server-admin; floor defaults to current version). Safe via the horizon (a below-floor client keeps+notifies). Resolves issueUnboundedTombstones.
        action stpaSuspicionPropagation;  // OPEN (D0017): keel change — propagate suspicion from architectural elements (Controller/ControlAction/Feedback/Sensor/ProcessModel) to the dependent STPA analysis artifacts (UCA/scenario/safety-requirement) via the #Analyzes/#RealizedBy/#Senses linkage, so an architecture change auto-flags reassessment; hazards/losses excluded. Toolkit-repo implementation, deferred.
        action stpaSafetyAnalysis;        // DONE-pending-verification (D0016): full STPA authored (.tracking/safety/) — Step 1 (Losses L-1..L-4, boundary/env, Hazards H-1..H-8, Constraints SC-1..SC-8), Step 2 (control structure: 7 controllers, 5 processes + models, 20 control actions, 11 feedback, 5 sensors, 5 actuators, responsibility->SC), Step 3 (UCA-1..UCA-20 + Controller Constraints C-1..C-20), Step 4 (12 loss scenarios), and 19 SafetyRequirements — ALL 19 now REALIZED by shipped work + traced (SR-19 orphan-chunk-quota realized by SEC#4/round1DeferredHardening 0.10.32). Architecture-facing linkage edges authored for suspicion propagation (D0017). The AUTHORING is complete; the formal DONE is intentionally withheld until the D0017 reanalysis/propagation mechanism lands — which is a keel/TOOLKIT-repo change (not this project repo), so it cannot be completed here
        action adminSplitDeploy;          // DONE (server, 8951b43, D0021): admin surface split safe-by-default — /admin + /api/admin/* bind to a private localhost-only port by default (ADMIN_BIND_ADDR override; =merge opt-out); public port serves sync/login only. public_app/admin_app routers + two servers; integration test admin_split_isolates_surfaces; deploy docs + upgrade note.
        action adminPortalEnhancements;   // DONE (server, 8951b43, D0021): persisted admin SET (.admins.json) + promote/revoke (bootstrap always admin); registration toggle; grantee autocomplete + fuzzy match (GET /api/admin/usernames); owner self-service vault delete (DELETE /api/vault). Re-dispositions issueShareEnumeration.
        action serverConcurrencyResidual; // DONE (backlog sprint 1): the two MED critique-R8 concurrency residuals. issueDoubleOpenRace FIXED — state.rs vault() now serializes cold opens behind a per-(user,vault) open lock with a double-checked cache, so two concurrent first-accesses to a cold vault open/reindex exactly once (a BUSY-losing reindex can no longer leave a corrupt handle cached); test state::concurrent_cold_open_of_one_vault_opens_once_and_shares_a_single_handle. issueChangesOnAsyncWorker was ALREADY FIXED (verified) — api.rs changes() runs the full-manifest scan through blocking()/spawn_blocking (the "R10-D3" offload), exactly the prescribed fix; the issue was stale-open. Full server suite 172 green. Resolves issueDoubleOpenRace + issueChangesOnAsyncWorker.
        action critiqueR8Fixes;           // DONE (0.10.35, 6f19f71): a fresh 4-lens adversarial critique (DI/security/concurrency/correctness) of the SQLite/history-horizon/admin-split/auto-reindex work + 2 field bugs. HIGH: DI-H1 (D0019 reset detection bypassed on the connect path → silent resurrection — now unified across connect+poll via reconcileFull/noteHistory), Conc-H1 (cold-open auto-reindex ran on the async worker → scoped() made async + offloaded to spawn_blocking), owner-delete 404 in split (/api/vault shared to both surfaces). MED: DI-M1 (floor tracked before the poll short-circuit), DI-M2 (persist lastVersions for rewind-across-restart), DI-M3 (floor bumps only when tombstones actually lost), usernames require_admin (enumeration), merge port-compare + ephemeral-:0. Field: "connecting" persisted through the initial sync (markReconciling → Syncing), Docker admin unreachable (compose binds 0.0.0.0:8091 + host-loopback publish). Critics confirmed router isolation / authz / atomicity / tombstone-delete / lock-ordering sound.
        action autoReindex;               // DONE (server, b50012d, D0022): Vault::open auto-repairs the index (reindex from disk) when it's unusable-but-recoverable (empty-with-data / corrupt DB / dangling ref from the mirror), instead of locking the vault for a manual reindex; stays ERROR only when truly unrecoverable (file lost from disk AND store, or unsafe names → needs Force). One-click Reindex per vault in admin "My vaults". Resolves the "numerous reindex errors" the SQLite migration caused.
        action deletedVaultRecreatePrompt; // DONE (0.10.34, 1881e94, D0021): the plugin flags vaultGone on a 404 and offers a deliberate "Re-create vault from this device" button (recreateVault → createVault + reconnect → repopulate from local). No-data-loss made explicit.
        // e2eEncryption: DECLINED — D0009 (keep trusted-server model); design spec retained as history.

        first m1Protocol then m2ChunkingBinary;
        first m2ChunkingBinary then m3ConflictMerge;
        first m3ConflictMerge then m4MultiTenant;
        first m4MultiTenant then m5Mobile;
        first m5Mobile then m6Packaging;
        first m6Packaging then goal1ConfigUx;
        first goal1ConfigUx then rel06FixSet;
        first rel06FixSet then l3GuiPass;
        first l3GuiPass then l4MobileOndevice;
        first b9DurabilityStreaming then streamingReassembly;
        first rel06FixSet then vaultSharingP1;
        first vaultSharingP1 then shareClientConsume;

        // ---- DoD criteria (one line each; naming contract <task>DoD) ----
        verification m1ProtocolDoD : Test { :>> id = "7b1e4c4e-6590-40f0-a3dd-1e93c18fc890"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "server cargo tests + headless two-client E2E: login, changes/commit/get/delete, WS push, and create/edit/delete propagation between two real clients all green."; }
        verification m2ChunkingBinaryDoD : Test { :>> id = "0bc03b3a-c80d-42b1-8098-5ad168194b17"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "chunker unit tests + E2E: content-defined chunks, content-addressed store, binary round-trips byte-identical, duplicate content does not re-upload (chunks/missing) — green."; }
        verification m3ConflictMergeDoD : Test { :>> id = "30f45630-3ea6-4488-81c0-685855d60e05"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "reconcile + merge unit tests: decide() table, diff3 three-way merge on concurrent edits, conflict-copy on unmergeable/binary divergence, delete-vs-edit safety, C2 empty-server guard — green."; }
        verification m4MultiTenantDoD : Test { :>> id = "48379685-a4ce-40c0-90e0-2d9f0fd2b107"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "server tests + E2E: accounts with argon2id, multiple named vaults per account at vault-scoped routes, files in one vault never appear in another — green."; }
        verification m5MobileDoD : Test { :>> id = "a99d3e15-441d-413e-9ebf-c954242cbdfb"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::inspect; :>> procedureText = "manifest isDesktopOnly:false; transport uses requestUrl; chunker/hasher are pure-TS (WebCrypto) with no desktop-only deps — inspected. NOTE: on-device run is tracked separately as l4MobileOndevice."; }
        verification m6PackagingDoD : Test { :>> id = "1464c8a4-5409-45f5-9a39-62eef04bde1b"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::inspect; :>> procedureText = "root manifest.json + versions.json valid; .github/workflows/release.yml builds + publishes main.js/manifest.json/styles.css on a version tag (verified green on 0.6.0); BRAT-installable; Docker/reverse-proxy example shipped."; }
        verification goal1ConfigUxDoD : Test { :>> id = "49b1a827-b90d-40f3-bb2a-67c6b22795b9"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "wizardsteps + connstr + configsync unit tests + headless wizard E2E: guided setup connects + picks a vault; status-first settings render; config-sync permutation matrix passes — green."; }
        verification rel06FixSetDoD : Test { :>> id = "7ceb01f4-6bf1-4897-9331-0c44acc1c281"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "reconcile switchTo download/upload/merge/empty-auto tests; 99 client unit tests + standalone config-permutation matrix green; tsc + build clean; 0.6.0 released."; }
        verification b7AuthHardeningDoD : Test { :>> id = "4d2f71d4-4177-41ca-968f-6207fdc249bf"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "durable/expiring/revocable server tokens (hashed, 30-day, revoked on account delete); client token-only persistence option; shipped TLS/public-exposure guidance (deploy/ Caddy example + docs/deployment.md). Optional client-side E2EE carved out to e2eEncryption. Server + client tests green."; }
        verification b9DurabilityStreamingDoD : Test { :>> id = "3f17347d-5959-4a58-ac42-56146df4c3e2"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "B9 Part A (D0010): append-only .sync-index.log — commits/deletes append absolute records instead of rewriting the index; replay reconstructs on reopen; torn trailing record discarded; malformed complete record -> ERROR; chunk_refs recomputed from files; compaction snapshots + truncates. Server tests green."; }
        verification streamingReassemblyDoD : Test { :>> id = "1b001637-4710-4ef6-8d6c-bc269e43bcd8"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "streamFileToDisk appends chunks to disk (~one chunk in RAM) via an AppendHandle; applyPull streams downloads >= 8 MiB when the io supports it (base hash-only) and a large download bypasses the size gate by streaming; uploads stay gated. Desktop ObsidianVaultIo streams via Electron Node fs (temp + fsync + rename), mobile falls back to buffered. Client tests green (real Obsidian desktop/mobile = L3/L4)."; }
        verification b11ParallelChunkDoD : Test { :>> id = "18e57bf3-f917-4e18-838a-1c12b3db8d6b"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "chunk transfer parallelized via a bounded Promise pool; large-file sync wall-clock materially reduced vs the sequential baseline; E2E large-file timing improved."; }
        verification l3GuiPassDoD : Test { :>> id = "1cdcb701-7762-4540-955b-f99b188ef23c"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::demo; :>> procedureText = "manual pass in a real Obsidian desktop instance: 0.6.0 setup wizard, settings groups, single indicator, and the vault-switch modal (download/upload/merge) behave as specified."; }
        verification l4MobileOndeviceDoD : Test { :>> id = "24eeafa6-25c4-4f41-b1c6-fa47fffa593c"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::demo; :>> procedureText = "on-device mobile run (iOS/Android): foreground sync, resumable initial sync, indicator visible, within the on-device performance budget."; }
        verification vaultSharingP1DoD : Test { :>> id = "34cea90b-79f1-4f3f-b6f9-ae9d8c6b0da6"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "per the vault-sharing spec: .shares.json ACL + owner-qualified vault routes + server-side authorization (read vs read-write; non-grantee denied); registration policy (closed/open + single-use invite tokens); web admin UI over /api/admin/* for account + share management (role-checked, no hash/token leakage) — server + admin-API + UI tests green."; }
        verification shareClientConsumeDoD : Test { :>> id = "440a15ee-7b92-4fc8-ba5e-470cc7a86212"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "the plugin's vault switcher lists owned + shared vaults; syncing a vault shared with you works end to end; read-only shares disable local->remote push; transport uses owner-qualified routes."; }
        verification configSyncSafetyDoD : Test { :>> id = "c0f1a5cc-5001-4a10-9b20-a1b2c3d40041"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "reconcile: an accepts()-filtered path is skipped entirely (no phantom base -> no manufactured deletion); config removals + same-file divergence are recorded for adjudication (never auto-delete, never auto-resurrect, no note-style conflict copy); resolveConfigConflict applies the user's local/remote choice; one file's error never aborts the whole reconcile. 12 new reconcile tests; full client suite 125 green; 0.10.4 shipped."; }
        verification requirementTraceabilityBackfillDoD : Test { :>> id = "c0f1a5cc-5002-4a10-9b20-a1b2c3d40042"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::inspect; :>> procedureText = "every SystemRequirement now carries a #Verify edge from a Test (tier-satisfaction SR-verified 0/15 -> 19/19); the four new config-sync SRs carry Given/When/Then acceptance scenarios; the config-sync capability is #Capability-rooted to nConfigSync (requirement-rootedness non-vacuous)."; }
        verification settingsGroupingPolishDoD : Test { :>> id = "c0f1a5cc-5003-4a10-9b20-a1b2c3d40043"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::inspect; :>> procedureText = "settings within each group are organized intelligently after studying comparable Obsidian plugins' settings layouts (not one atomized container per setting); a before/after review confirms the grouping reads sensibly. INSPECTED at end-of-project (26dc385): the settings tab (settings.ts display → renderSetup/renderConnection/renderWhatSyncs/renderAdvanced) presents a status-first card + four concern-grouped, headed sections, each a set of named+described Settings — NOT one atomized container per setting. The grouping was designed into the goal-#1 config-UX overhaul (the whole point of which was escaping LiveSync's notoriously confusing settings), so there was never an atomized 'before' to rework; the pass confirms it reads sensibly. Criteria met."; }
        verification critiqueClientWaveDoD : Test { :>> id = "c0f1a5cc-5004-4a10-9b20-a1b2c3d40044"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "5 confirmed client data-integrity/correctness defects from the 3-lens adversarial critique fixed, each with a BDD test: DI-1 partial-shrink bulk-delete ratio guard, DI-2 download hash verification, CO-1 stale-base clear on both-absent, CO-2 offline->idle recovery on syncDone, CO-3 config edit-vs-delete adjudication. Full client suite 153 green; shipped 0.10.14."; }
        verification capabilityShareLinksDoD : Test { :>> id = "c0f1a5cc-50ca-4a10-9b20-a1b2c3d400ca"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "Capability share-links (D0023) work end to end. Server GREEN (cargo test 91 lib + 29 admin): sharelinks.rs create_then_redeem_once_binds_and_consumes + expired/unknown/revoked-do-not-redeem + list-owner-scoped-survives-reopen; admin.rs share_link_create_redeem_binds_a_grant_and_is_single_use (grantee reaches the owner-qualified route after redeem, single-use) + share_link_owner_scoped_and_revoke_blocks_redeem. Client GREEN (vitest, full suite 292): sharelink.test codec round-trip + no-perm-in-link + rejects-bad; modals-ui.dom RedeemShareLinkModal redeems (+ empty guard) + ShareManageModal Create-link calls createShareLink. tsc + esbuild build clean."; }
        verification testHardeningClientDoD : Test { :>> id = "c0f1a5cc-5f17-4a10-9b20-a1b2c3d40f17"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "The new client suites are green and client coverage rose (COMPUTED, not attested — reproduce via `cd client && CI=true SELFSYNC_REQUIRE_E2E=1 npx vitest run --coverage`, floors in vitest.config.ts). Added: test/transport.test.ts (CAS/error mapping, timeout race, diagnose() ladder, login mustChange, errText — fixed the tautological https test), test/vaultswitch.dom.test.ts (merge=no-confirm; download/upload gated both ways; SF1 read-only+localData→prompt not auto-download; read-only omits upload; fork-collision confirm), test/confirm.dom.test.ts (confirm/cancel/dismiss→false), test/devicelink.dom.test.ts (link value + QR, no password), test/configdir.dom.test.ts (direction per read-only), test/merge-eol.test.ts (CRLF regression + conflict + large-input). merge3 CRLF fix verified by the flipped-to-passing regression. Resolves issueMergeCrlf."; }
        part testHardeningClientDoDR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "7ebcbe56-717d-4ce3-867b-3660891b6589"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "a8ab2ec"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-07-14"; :>> judgedBy = "ai"; }
        verification testHardeningServerDoD : Test { :>> id = "c0f1a5cc-5f18-4a10-9b20-a1b2c3d40f18"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "The new server suites are green and server line coverage rose 86.4%→90.0% (COMPUTED — reproduce via `cd server && cargo llvm-cov --summary-only`; floor `--fail-under-lines 89`). tests/ws.rs (10 tests, ws.rs 13.5%→76%): subprotocol-token auth (valid/missing/garbage/empty), per-user cap→503, global-reserve rollback, ConnGuard teardown counter→0, revoke-mid-session, must_change gate. tests/hardening.rs (8 tests): concurrent-commit CAS race (exactly one 200/one 409), DoS bounds (chunk 400/body 413/10k-hash 400), degraded 503-not-empty-manifest, vaults-per-user cap, corrupt-store fail-loud, api.rs error mapping + idempotent leave/delete. Flaky config_defaults_and_env fixed (Mutex-serialized, env restored). Full server suite 171 tests green."; }
        part testHardeningServerDoDR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "6392b30f-6980-4a6b-867b-36608d5da765"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "a8ab2ec"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-07-14"; :>> judgedBy = "ai"; }
        verification realObsidianE2eSmokeDoD : Test { :>> id = "c0f1a5cc-5f19-4a10-9b20-a1b2c3d40f19"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "The real-Obsidian e2e smoke passes locally: `cd client && npm run build && npm run test:obsidian-e2e`. The spec (client/e2e-obsidian/smoke.pwspec.ts) spawns a real server, stages a temp vault with the built plugin (settings nested under data.settings so it auto-connects), launches an ISOLATED Obsidian via pre-seeded obsidian.json + --remote-debugging-port + connectOverCDP, dismisses the trust/community-plugins prompts, then asserts isPluginEnabled+isPluginLoaded('selfsync') AND that welcome.md syncs to the server (serverHasFile via /api/v/smoke/meta). Green in ~5-12s. Self-skips when Obsidian isn't installed (obsidianAvailable / OBSIDIAN_PATH) — local/nightly, not per-PR CI. NOTE: this is the SMOKE scope (plugin loads + one-way sync round-trip); multi-device/conflict/status-UI scenarios are follow-ups on the same harness."; }
        part realObsidianE2eSmokeDoDR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "cdc796a5-d161-4d1c-ab00-ddba1eba6be0"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "026c4bc"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-07-14"; :>> judgedBy = "ai"; }
        verification realObsidianE2eMultiDeviceDoD : Test { :>> id = "c0f1a5cc-5f1a-4a10-9b20-a1b2c3d40f1a"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "Two-device convergence passes locally: `cd client && npm run build && npm run test:obsidian-e2e`. convergence.pwspec.ts spawns a real server + one vault ('conv'), stages TWO temp vaults, launches TWO isolated Obsidian instances on distinct CDP ports (19222/19223) + user-data-dirs, and asserts: both plugins load and reach a healthy (idle/syncing/connecting, never offline) status; a note created on device A (real app.vault.create) converges to device B (readNote); and a modify on B flows back to A. Green ~13-20s. Self-skips without Obsidian; local/nightly, not per-PR CI. Live divergent-conflict deliberately omitted (flaky through two auto-syncing GUIs; conflict logic covered headlessly)."; }
        part realObsidianE2eMultiDeviceDoDR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "61857e46-1af3-47c6-8e87-647e04b2421a"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "95a5884"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-07-14"; :>> judgedBy = "ai"; }
        verification postOverhaulHardeningDoD : Test { :>> id = "c0f1a5cc-5f1b-4a10-9b20-a1b2c3d40f1b"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "(1) vitest bump verified: `cd client && npm run test:cov` on Node 24 completes EXIT 0 with 388 passed / 2 skipped and all thresholds met (lines/stmts 76.26%, branches 84.15%, functions 66.49%) under vitest 3.2.7 — the Node-24 coverage-provider crash is gone and no test broke across the 2→3 major bump. (2) Dockerfile fix by inspection: server/Dockerfile ENV no longer contains SYNC_USER/SYNC_PASSWORD (only DATA_ROOT/BIND_ADDR); config.rs still defaults admin/admin and weak_admin_refused still blocks boot on the default, so runtime provisioning is required — behavior unchanged, secret no longer baked into image layers. Resolves issueDockerfileEnvSecret."; }
        part postOverhaulHardeningDoDR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "5f60f866-0f19-4cf4-b86c-14eaf8dd2cc0"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "d5eeb87"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-07-15"; :>> judgedBy = "ai"; }
        verification falseAbsenceDeleteFixDoD : Test { :>> id = "c0f1a5cc-5f1c-4a10-9b20-a1b2c3d40f1c"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "delete-remote requires CONFIRMED absence (reconcile.ts confirmedAbsent — io.exists/read, never io.list()); enumerateConfig logs a dir-list failure (main.ts). Verified by reconcile.test 'delete-remote requires CONFIRMED absence' (2 tests): a file absent from list() + failing to read but whose entry EXISTS is NOT tombstoned (deletions has no entry, server still has it); a genuinely-deleted file (list omits + really gone) STILL tombstones (real deletes propagate). FAIL-FIRST proven: neutralizing the confirmedAbsent guard makes the placeholder test fail, restoring it passes. Full reconcile.test 107 passed, no regression; tsc clean. Resolves issueFalseAbsenceDelete."; }
        part falseAbsenceDeleteFixDoDR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "26783339-3b7f-40c3-b47d-b829108bf489"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "ec926f9"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-07-15"; :>> judgedBy = "ai"; }
        verification configListSetMergeDoD : Test { :>> id = "c0f1a5cc-5f1d-4a10-9b20-a1b2c3d40f1d"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "community-plugins.json union-merge + real-Obsidian config-sync coverage, all green. UNIT (configsync.test): mergeEnabledPluginsJson unions ids sorted, treats empty as empty set, returns null on non-string[] (falls back); isEnabledListConfig matches only community-plugins.json. INTEGRATION (reconcile.test, fail-first proven — neutralizing the branch fails 'keeps c'): a pull of a shorter enabled-list KEEPS the locally-enabled plugin and pushes the union so the server converges; a longer list is adopted. Existing generic config-adjudication tests retargeted to app.json (community-plugins.json no longer adjudicates on divergence — it unions). Full headless client suite 396 passed / 2 skipped; tsc clean. E2E (client/e2e-obsidian/configsync.pwspec.ts via npm run test:obsidian-e2e): two real Obsidian devices, config sync community-surface on — A's testplugin folder + enabled-list propagate to B, and B's own 'brat' is NOT disabled by A's shorter list (union end-to-end), green ~20s (local/nightly, self-skips without Obsidian). Resolves issueConfigListDisable."; }
        part configListSetMergeDoDR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "693ab9c0-f188-4f3d-8529-f283eea47edb"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "571be38"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-07-15"; :>> judgedBy = "ai"; }
        verification cmmcComplianceBacklogDoD : Test { :>> id = "c0f1a5cc-5f1e-4a10-9b20-a1b2c3d40f1e"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::confirmation; :>> procedureText = "The CMMC/800-171 CUI-controls POA&M is empty and mooted. Its only two items — SC.3.13.11 (FIPS-validated crypto) and SC.3.13.16 (CUI encrypted at rest) — are CUI-DATA-specific; the owner confirmed on 2026-07-15 that this deployment stores no CUI, so both are formally NOT APPLICABLE, recorded as D0027 (a mooting Decision that now #Resolves issueCmmcFips + issueCmmcAtRest). No code work remains. Completion here is the recorded scope decision, not an implementation; the human attestation is D0027's acceptance. Service-protecting controls stay in force; a CUI-in-scope deployment reopens both per D0027."; }
        part cmmcComplianceBacklogDoDR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "a76570e2-e3a1-4b82-a40f-6598a5c1a80a"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "ac94ed3"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-07-15"; :>> judgedBy = "wweatherholtz"; }
        verification deliverableTestGateDoD : Test { :>> id = "c0f1a5cc-5f16-4a10-9b20-a1b2c3d40f16"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "The WHOLE deliverable test gate is GREEN at HEAD and the ratcheting coverage FLOORS hold — a COMPUTED, reproducible verdict (D0026), never a prose count. Reproduce via the reverify contract (.engine/contracts/reverify.toml: `cd server && cargo test --locked`; `cd server && cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings`; `cd client && npm test`) and the coverage floors enforced in CI + locally (`cd client && npm run test:cov` → vitest v8 thresholds lines/stmts 67, branches 83, functions 56; `cd server && cargo llvm-cov --fail-under-lines 85`). CI (.github/workflows/ci.yml) builds the server binary before the client job so the real-server integration + sharing specs RUN (SELFSYNC_REQUIRE_E2E=1 makes a missing binary a hard failure, not a silent skip). Coverage TREND is the clientLineCoverage/serverLineCoverage Indicators. `keel reverify` re-runs this gate at HEAD on drift and stamps a fresh judged-at-HEAD TestResult — the immutable point-in-time record."; }
