        // ===== Design-pattern conformance critique (2026-07-19): 3 OPEN follow-on actions. Findings from
        // 5 independent conformance critics over the 27 pattern-tagged CodeElements (verified against code). =====
        action patternConformanceHardening;
        verification patternConformanceHardeningDoD : Test { :>> id = "9a77e001-1b2c-4d3e-8f40-5a6b7c8d9e01"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "DONE (reverify green @ f96b217, deliverableTestGate: server cargo test --locked + clippy -D warnings + client vitest 453): implemented all four resolved issues, each behaviour-preserving + tested — (1) validateFileMeta now validates mtime via asNum + constructs (no cast); (2) SafeName newtype (users.rs) + SafeVaultPath brand (pathsafe.ts, the raw-fs join gated via rawFsAbs) + ServerOrigin refined type (connstr.ts, cleartext verdict parsed once); (3) reconcileOne→pure finalize()→ReconcileEffect + reconcileMergeOrConflict→pure planMerge()→MergePlan + acceptedBasePaths() guard-denominator dedup + item-4 (confirmedAbsent→ProbedPresence tagged type, mapPool shared abort flag, ContentStore put-vs-remove contract doc); (4) ChunkHash newtype + conflictCopyIfRaced RaceOutcome union + parseSettings() parser + OpenLockReaper RAII guard + AuditAction/Outcome catalog newtypes. Commits 59a7613..f96b217. ORIGINAL PLAN follows. (1) DEFECT issueValidateFileMetaMtimeUnchecked — validateFileMeta (protocol.ts:52) validates path/hash/size/version/chunks but NOT mtime, yet returns `o as FileMeta` asserting mtime:number; a hostile server's mtime:'evil'/NaN passes + flows into base stat-stamping. Fix: add asNum(m.mtime) + construct-don't-cast (like validateStatus). (2) issueBoolPredicatesNoRefinedType — turn bool safety-predicates into refined/branded types so the checked property is type-carried, not re-asserted at every call site: safe_name (users.rs, re-checked ~20 sites incl. a double-check on register — a SafeName newtype whose only ctor parses; highest ROI since the name becomes an FS segment), isSafeVaultPath (5 client I/O sites → branded SafeVaultPath), isInsecureRemote (4 sites → fold the verdict into normalizeServer's refined ServerOrigin). (3) issueFunctionalCoreShellsReDecide — widen the pure core: reconcileOne → a pure finalize(action, facts)→Effect (lift config re-adjudication + guard gating out of the shell; resolve confirmedAbsent/exists to booleans first), reconcileMergeOrConflict → a pure MergePlan value (shell only executes writes), reconcilePath → a shared perPassDeleteGuard helper (dedup the runDeleteGuard drift, B1). (4) low: ContentStore::put — document/guard the put-vs-remove concurrency contract (safety currently BORROWED from the Vault RwLock + orphan-TTL across 3 files, not enforced in the store); confirmedAbsent → return LocalContent/Presence not bool; mapPool — a shared abort flag if a non-idempotent caller ever appears (today safe by idempotency). Resolves issueValidateFileMetaMtimeUnchecked + issueBoolPredicatesNoRefinedType + issueFunctionalCoreShellsReDecide + issuePatternUntaggedShouldAdopt."; }
        part patternConformanceHardeningDoDR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "9a77e001-1b2c-4d3e-8f40-5a6b7c8d9e05"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "f96b217"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-07-19"; :>> judgedBy = "claudeOpus"; }
        action stateMachineConsolidation;
