        verification releaseCurrencyGuardDoD : Test { :>> id = "9a77e004-1b2c-4d3e-8f40-5a6b7c8d9e07"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "DONE (D0033 accepted + shipped @ 0b69885): added scripts/check-release-currency.mjs (counts unreleased shippable-path commits since the last release tag; WARN>=1, FAIL >10 commits or >14 days), wired into verify-released.yml (daily net), + process step rv6Currency + release-versioning skill doc-sync. Verified: reports 0 now (post-1.6.1) and 47 over the pre-release range (would have hard-failed as overdue). keel guard ALL PASS. ORIGINAL PLAN follows. Add a release-CURRENCY assertion. Today check-release.mjs + verify-released.yml only assert the MANIFEST's version is tagged + published — satisfied whenever the manifest points at a released version, EVEN IF main has drifted far past it. That is exactly why 48 shippable commits (of 100 total; 52 were .engine/.tracking/docs-only) piled up unreleased since 1.6.0 while both checks stayed green. Fix (mirrors D0012's repo-local, out-of-keel-scope pattern): a scripts/check-release-currency.mjs that counts main commits since the last release tag touching SHIPPABLE paths (client/**, server/**, manifest.json, versions.json — NOT engine/tracking/docs, else every stamp/CR false-positives), WARNs at >=1 unreleased shippable commit and FAILs past a threshold (~10 commits or ~14 days), wired into the daily .github/workflows/verify-released.yml net so the drift goes visible on its own. Resolves issueReleaseCurrencyBlindSpot."; }
