        verification timestampIgnoreRedesignDoD : Test { :>> id = "d7c19006-0000-4a10-9b20-a1b2c3d40096"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "Ships MINOR 1.9.0. SelfSync writes NO note timestamps (seed/conform/backfill/stamp/drive-fs/restore-detection deleted; timestampBackfill.ts + fstimes.ts removed). Content identity ALWAYS normalizes EOL/BOM/trailing-newline for all text files (the CRLF-false-positive fix — normalizedHash no longer short-circuits to the raw hash for a no-frontmatter note); when the feature is on it additionally masks timestamp-VALUED frontmatter keys, VALUE-SHAPE gated (a non-date value under an ignored key still syncs) and PATTERN matched (updated-* per-device keys). Applied as a post-decide client-side override (server/manifest hash stays raw; base keeps {raw hash, normHash}) so pending-counts / delete-detection / CAS are unaffected. Hardened by 3 independent antagonistic critiques: merge3 neutralizes+restores timestamp lines (a real body merge isn't spoiled -> no spurious conflict copy); delete-local uses normHash equality (a peer deletion is honored, not resurrected); convergence keeps local bytes (no rewrite loop with an auto-timestamp plugin). Settings pivot embeddedTimestamps->ignoreTimestampChanges (default ON, identity-only, no counted-consent) with automatic migration. Guard (D0047): the redesign's own vitest cases (CRLF-only-not-pushed, timestamp-only-no-copy, Finding-B merge, Finding-C delete-local) + value-shape/pattern frontmatter tests. DoD: full client vitest (501) + tsc --noEmit clean + keel validate + guard green. Server untouched. Resolves issueTimestampFabricatedCreated + issueTimestampBackfillConflictFlood + issueCrlfFalsePositiveChanges (superseding the embeddedTimestampMetadata approach to issueTimestampConflictNoise)."; }
