        // ===== Sprint streamedPullRacingEditGuard (2026-08-02) — 1.12.1: close SR-2's accepted streamed-pull
        // residual (a mid-stream local edit lost on a >=8 MiB pull, L-1). Found by the chunking STPA-hunt. =====
        action streamedPullRacingEditGuard;
        verification streamedPullRacingEditGuardDoD : Test { :>> id = "4d9e2b70-6c81-4f35-a2c6-1e0f39a57b48"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "Ships PATCH 1.12.1 (DATA-INTEGRITY, L-1; client-only, NO server redeploy). The client chunking/reassembly STPA-UCA hunt (independent critic) found the one real unrecoverable-loss window in the subsystem: applyPull's streamed branch (rmeta.size >= 8 MiB) checked for a racing local edit BEFORE streaming, then streamFileToDisk reassembled to a temp + atomic-renamed over `path` in close() with NO seam re-check — so an edit saved DURING the multi-second download was clobbered and base set to remote (next reconcile: local==base==in-sync -> edit gone). The buffered path (< 8 MiB notes) already re-checks after the fetch; this was the asymmetry, and EXACTLY SR-2's documented 'Residual (accepted): sub-window TOCTOU on very large streamed pulls'. The owner chose to fix (streamedPullRacingEditGuardChoice). FIX: streamFileToDisk gains a beforeRename hook (after the incremental hash-verify, before close()'s rename); applyPull passes a seam guard reusing conflictCopyIfRaced on the ORIGINAL on-disk file (still holds the racing edit — NOT the post-rename result, so base is only ever rmeta.hash; this is why the retired 'post-write re-read' regressed and this doesn't). A >8 MiB config race throws StreamRaceAbort -> adjudicate, never overwrite. An independent critic (SOUND-WITH-CHANGES) caught a follow-on hole -> the fix does NOT delete the seam copy on a post-beforeRename failure (a post-rename close() throw would leave the copy the SOLE surviving edit), plus a close()-must-never-throw-after-rename contract. Guards (fail-first): reconcile.test 'preserves a mid-stream local edit as a conflict copy', 'makes NO spurious copy when there is no racing edit', 'a >8 MiB CONFIG file edited mid-stream ABORTS (adjudicate)', 'a close() failure AFTER the rename does NOT delete the sole surviving racing edit'. DoD: full client vitest (559) + tsc clean + esbuild build clean + keel validate/guard green. Resolves issueStreamedPullMidEditLoss; closes SR-2's streamed-pull residual (STPA S-3 / UCA-4)."; }
        part streamedPullRacingEditGuardDoDR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "5e0f3c81-7d92-4046-b3d7-2f1a40b68c59"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "a347bf8"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-08-02"; :>> judgedBy = "claudeOpus"; }
        // The owner's DESIGN CHOICE (confirmation) — fix over accept-the-residual; their word is the evidence.
        verification streamedPullRacingEditGuardChoice : Test { :>> id = "6f1a4d92-8e03-4157-c4e8-30256bc79d6a"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::confirmation; :>> procedureText = "The owner was shown the VERIFIED finding — a mid-stream local edit unrecoverably lost on a >=8 MiB streamed pull, the buffered path already safe, the window narrow + currently an accepted residual, closable but in a seam that regressed once — and chose 'Fix it (careful spec + critique + TDD)' over 'Keep the accepted residual' and 'Write the diff for review first', via an explicit AskUserQuestion on 2026-08-02. This records ONLY that design-approach choice (their word is the evidence, D0016); it is NOT acceptance of the shipped RESULT — sittingReview20260802d covers the owner's review of 1.12.1."; }
        part streamedPullRacingEditGuardChoiceR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "7a2b5e03-9f14-4268-d5f9-41367cd8ae7b"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "a347bf8"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-08-02"; :>> judgedBy = "wweatherholtz"; }
