        // ===== Sprint persistScanSkipHint (2026-08-02) — 1.12.2: persist the (size,mtime) scan-skip hint so a
        // plugin reload doesn't re-hash the whole vault (owner field report; reverses R15 sync#3). =====
        action persistScanSkipHint;
        verification persistScanSkipHintDoD : Test { :>> id = "5e0a3c81-7d92-4f46-b3d8-2f1a40c67b59"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "Ships PATCH 1.12.2 (perf/UX; client-only, NO server redeploy). Owner-reported via the 1.12.0 connect timing: every fresh 'plugin loaded' re-reads+re-hashes the whole vault (~1137 files) on the first connect though nothing changed. Cause: BaseStore.toJSON persisted only hash/text/normHash, DROPPING the (size,mtime) scan-skip hint (R15 sync#3, 'never let a perf hint outlive its verifying session'), so a reload had no stamps and reconcileOne re-hashed every file. OWNER DECISION (AskUserQuestion 'Persist the scan-skip hints', recorded in persistScanSkipHintChoice): persist size+mtime. FIX (minimal): toJSON emits size+mtime (the constructor already loads them; main.ts already round-trips base.toJSON through saveData/loadData) -> baseStatUnchanged matches on reload -> the read+SHA-256 is skipped for unchanged files. Independent critic verdict SOUND (no data-loss path): under a scan-hit decide() can only return in-sync or pull (every destructive action needs L!=B, but the scan-hit pins L=B); the one mutating path (pull) re-reads live in applyPull->conflictCopyIfRaced, so even a LYING stamp colliding with a remote change writes a conflict copy, never a silent overwrite; remote changes are detected via the manifest regardless. Accepted (widened) residual: a mtime-preserving out-of-band edit isn't re-hashed until the next edit event / size|mtime change / remote divergence (the reload full-rehash backstop is removed) — a DELAY, never loss. Guards (fail-first): base.test 'PERSISTS the (size,mtime) scan-skip hint through toJSON/reload'; reconcile T2/T5 'an unchanged file skips the read AND does nothing', T3 'a STALE stamp does NOT mask a changed file', T4 (safety) 'a LYING stamp colliding with a remote change makes a CONFLICT COPY, never a silent overwrite', T6 'a persisted stamp for an ABSENT local file does NOT mask the deletion'; + a main.ts mtime-source-parity invariant comment (T7). DoD: full client vitest (563) + tsc clean + esbuild build clean + keel validate/guard green. Resolves issueScanSkipHintNotPersisted. (The ~18s .obsidian config-tree walk + the every-connect token re-login surfaced by the same log are SEPARATE, not in this sprint.)"; }
        part persistScanSkipHintDoDR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "6f1b4d92-8e03-4057-c4e9-30251bd78c6a"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "ab7e47e"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-08-02"; :>> judgedBy = "claudeOpus"; }
        // The owner's DESIGN CHOICE (confirmation) — persist over keep-dropping; their word is the evidence.
        verification persistScanSkipHintChoice : Test { :>> id = "7a2c5e03-9f14-4168-d5fa-41362ce89d7b"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::confirmation; :>> procedureText = "Shown that the whole-vault re-hash on every reload is because the (size,mtime) scan-skip hint is deliberately not persisted, and the tradeoff of persisting it (the accepted rsync/Syncthing residual, now spanning restarts), the owner chose 'Persist the scan-skip hints' over 'Chase the 18s config-tree walk instead' and 'Just fix the label + look at the token', via an explicit AskUserQuestion on 2026-08-02. This records ONLY that design-approach choice (their word is the evidence, D0016) — reversing R15 sync#3; it is NOT acceptance of the shipped RESULT (sittingReview20260802e)."; }
        part persistScanSkipHintChoiceR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "8b3d6f14-a025-4279-e6ab-52473def9c8d"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "ab7e47e"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-08-02"; :>> judgedBy = "wweatherholtz"; }
