        // ===== Sprint tokenIdleDefaultOff (2026-08-02) — 1.12.3: make the server session idle-timeout default-OFF
        // so the plugin stops re-logging in on every reopen after a break (owner field report). SERVER change. =====
        action tokenIdleDefaultOff;
        verification tokenIdleDefaultOffDoD : Test { :>> id = "6e1b4d92-8f03-4157-c4e9-30251be89d7c"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "Ships PATCH 1.12.3 (SERVER — the self-hosted server image MUST be redeployed to take effect; the plugin re-release is a no-op, client unchanged). Owner-reported via the 1.12.0 connect log: 'token rejected — re-logging in' on connect. Cause: the server's persisted bearer tokens (survive restart) carry a 30-day absolute cap AND an IDLE timeout (AC.3.1.11) that DEFAULTED to 30 min — a device closed/not-syncing for >30 min idle-expires, so the next open 401s + the client auto-relogins. OWNER DECISION (AskUserQuestion 'Default to the 30-day absolute cap (no idle expiry)', recorded in tokenIdleDefaultOffChoice): default idle expiry OFF. FIX: tokens.rs DEFAULT_IDLE_TTL_SECS 30*60 -> 0 (idle off; token lives its full 30-day absolute cap + revoke/password-change). The control REMAINS available — a compliance-seeking operator opts in via SESSION_IDLE_TIMEOUT_SECS=<positive>. COMPLIANCE reconciled honestly (D0098 — not silently): NIST 800-171 3.1.11 disposition partial->operator (opt-in) + 3.13.9's inactivity clause; docs/cmmc-posture.md + docs/deployment.md doc-synced (default-off + how to opt in). Guards (fail-first): server tokens.rs default_has_no_idle_expiry_only_the_absolute_cap (locks the new default: a long-idle token still resolves, the absolute cap still expires it) + idle_expires_a_stale_token_but_keeps_an_active_one (the control WHEN opted-in). DoD: full server cargo test (all suites 0 failed) + clippy clean + keel validate/guard green. Resolves issueTokenIdleReloginFriction. (The ~18s .obsidian config-tree walk from the same log is the NEXT sprint, owner 'then the other'.)"; }
        part tokenIdleDefaultOffDoDR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "7a2c5e03-9f14-4268-d5fa-41362cf89d8b"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "f7f7d05"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-08-02"; :>> judgedBy = "claudeOpus"; }
        // The owner's DESIGN CHOICE (confirmation) — default idle off over keep-30-min; their word is the evidence.
        verification tokenIdleDefaultOffChoice : Test { :>> id = "8b3d6f14-a025-4379-e6ab-52473def9c8e"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::confirmation; :>> procedureText = "Shown that the connect re-login is a 30-min session idle-timeout (AC.3.1.11) and the security-vs-convenience tradeoff, the owner chose 'Default to the 30-day absolute cap (no idle expiry)' over 'A longer idle default (7 days)' and 'Leave the default, just document the env var', via an explicit AskUserQuestion on 2026-08-02. This records ONLY that design-approach choice (their word is the evidence, D0016) — relaxing the out-of-box idle control (kept opt-in via SESSION_IDLE_TIMEOUT_SECS); it is NOT acceptance of the shipped RESULT (sittingReview20260802f)."; }
        part tokenIdleDefaultOffChoiceR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "9c4e7015-b136-4480-f7bd-63584efb0da0"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "f7f7d05"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-08-02"; :>> judgedBy = "wweatherholtz"; }
