        // ===== Sprint configWalkParallel (2026-08-02) — 1.12.4: parallelize the .obsidian config-tree walk
        // (the ~18s 'scanning local files' phase) under a bounded cap. Owner directed ('then the other'). =====
        action configWalkParallel;
        verification configWalkParallelDoD : Test { :>> id = "7f2c5e14-9a03-4268-b5da-41362cf89e8c"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "Ships PATCH 1.12.4 (perf; client-only, NO server redeploy). Owner-reported via the 1.12.0 connect timing: the 'scanning local files' phase took ~18s. Cause: ObsidianVaultIo.enumerateConfig walked the .obsidian tree FULLY SEQUENTIALLY (one awaited adapter.list/stat at a time, depth-first), so the wall-clock was (call COUNT x per-call latency) — brutal on a mobile latency-bound adapter, every reconcile. Owner directed the fix ('then the other'). FIX: extract the walk into a pure, unit-tested configwalk.ts (walkConfigTree) that runs adapter.list/stat CONCURRENTLY under a GLOBAL concurrency cap (CONFIG_ENUM_CONCURRENCY=12, a counting semaphore — a per-call mapPool can't bound a recursive walk), collapsing wall-clock toward (tree DEPTH x latency). Behavior-preserving + read-only: the SAME passing-file set (order-independent), an unlistable dir SKIPPED not treated-as-empty (+ logged; reconcile's per-file probe still guards a false delete), and a slow walk logs its shape ('config scan: N folders + M files in Xs') so the win is measurable on the next connect. Guards (configwalk.test): finds every passing file across a nested tree; respects the passes filter; a list error skips only that subtree + continues; NEVER exceeds the cap (peak<=limit) yet DID parallelize (peak>1); empty tree. DoD: full client vitest (566) + tsc clean + esbuild build clean + keel validate/guard green. Resolves issueConfigWalkSlow."; }
        part configWalkParallelDoDR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "8a3d6f25-ab14-4379-c6eb-52473df9af9d"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "d4cdd32"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-08-02"; :>> judgedBy = "claudeOpus"; }
        #Covers dependency from sittingReview20260802f to configWalkParallel;
        // ===== Sprint reconcileExamProgress (2026-08-02) — 1.12.5: honest 'checking N' label + live progress
        // for the connect examination (owner: 'says reconciling but not doing anything' / 'stuck on label'). =====
        action reconcileExamProgress;
        verification reconcileExamProgressDoD : Test { :>> id = "9b4d7136-ac15-4380-c6ec-52473e0abfad"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "Ships PATCH 1.12.5 (UX + DIAGNOSTIC; client-only, NO server redeploy). Owner-reported (field): the connect showed 'reconciling 1137 local file(s)' and appeared idle ('says reconciling but not doing anything'), then 'stuck on label'. Two issues: (1) the 1.12.0 sub-phase label 'reconciling N' read as 'syncing N' when the pass EXAMINES all files + transfers only what changed; (2) it was STATIC, so a slow full pass (a first-run re-hash before the 1.12.2 scan-skip stamps persist, or a large mobile vault) looked frozen and a hang was indistinguishable from slow. FIX: (a) honest label 'checking N files for changes' (real transfer work still shows as 'Syncing… N pending' via onProgress); (b) LIVE 'checked X/N files' progress (every 250 examined) so a slow pass shows MOVEMENT and a genuine hang is PINPOINTED (the count freezes at the stuck file). This is a UX + diagnostic fix — if the stall is a HARD hang (not a one-time slow re-hash that completes + persists stamps -> fast thereafter), the frozen count locates it for a targeted follow-up. Guards: reconcile.test onStage sequence updated (fetching -> scanning -> 'checking N files for changes'). DoD: full client vitest (566) + tsc clean + esbuild build clean + keel validate/guard green. Resolves issueReconcileExamOpaque."; }
        part reconcileExamProgressDoDR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "ac5e8247-bd16-4491-08cd-63584f0bcfbe"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "918974e"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-08-02"; :>> judgedBy = "claudeOpus"; }
        #Covers dependency from sittingReview20260802g to reconcileExamProgress;
        // ===== Sprint removePluginServerButton (2026-08-02) — 1.12.5: remove the per-plugin 'Remove from
        // server' button (owner: 'taking up far too much space for a rare need'). =====
        action removePluginServerButton;
        verification removePluginServerButtonDoD : Test { :>> id = "ad6f9358-ce27-45a2-19de-74695f1cd0cf"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::inspect; :>> procedureText = "Ships PATCH 1.12.5 (UI declutter; client-only). Owner-directed: 'get rid of the Remove from server button ... if the owner wants to remove packages, they can do so in the admin interface ... taking up far too much space for a rare need.' The settings plugin list rendered a 'Remove from server' button on EVERY server-present plugin row (settings.ts renderPluginRows) — a button per row for a rare, admin-appropriate need. FIX: remove the per-row button + its confirm/purge onClick. The plugin's removePluginFromServer method STAYS (still tested — plugin-wiring 'purges ONLY that plugin's server files' + 'REJECTS a traversal/malformed id'), just not surfaced as per-row UI. Verified by INSPECTION (a UI-space removal): tsc clean (no orphaned refs — onServer/manifests/confirmModal all used elsewhere), no test asserted the button, full client vitest (566) + DOM suites green. Resolves issuePluginRemoveButtonClutter."; }
        part removePluginServerButtonDoDR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "be7a0469-df38-4033-2aef-857a601de0d0"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "918974e"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-08-02"; :>> judgedBy = "claudeOpus"; }
