        // ===== Sprint wsSupersededGuard (2026-08-02) — 1.12.6: the WS-push STPA-UCA hunt's one real bug — the
        // open/error handlers lacked the superseded-socket identity guard that close has. =====
        action wsSupersededGuard;
        verification wsSupersededGuardDoD : Test { :>> id = "cf9c268b-f047-4144-3bf1-069c823f02f2"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "Ships PATCH 1.12.6 (client-only, NO server redeploy). An independent STPA-UCA hunt on the WS push path (server + client) found this ONE real defect (Medium): spinUpWs's `open`/`error` handlers lacked the `this.ws !== ws` superseded-socket guard that `close` + the liveness tick already apply — the FSM's own design (transportstate.ts:7) requires ALL socket events to honor it. So a late `error` from a SUPERSEDED old socket degraded the CURRENT live socket (realtimeConnected->false, yellow 'Synced (polling)' instead of green, poll pinned to 4s -> battery, no self-heal until the next socket cycle). Safe direction (no missed changes / no false-synced -> Medium), a clear asymmetric-guard bug. FIX: add the identity guard to both open + error, matching close. Guard (fail-first): plugin-wiring 'a SUPERSEDED WS socket's late open/error does NOT disturb the current live socket' (the harness fake WS made fireable). DoD: full client vitest (567) + tsc clean + esbuild build clean + keel validate/guard green. Resolves issueWsSupersededOpenError. HUNT RESULT: the WS path is otherwise well-defended — server side NULL on auth/isolation(per-vault channel, no cross-tenant leak)/notify/revoke(re-authed before every delivery)/bounds/close; client side NULL on token-handling/close-recovery/message-flood/false-live. The only other items are a LOW server defense-in-depth (issueWsSessionAliveMustChange, backlogged) + accepted tradeoffs (per-delivery re-auth amplification; a bounded transient false-green; a negligible shared lastWsActivity) — not defects."; }
        part wsSupersededGuardDoDR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "d0ad379c-0158-4255-4c02-17ad934013a3"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "0d02f1e"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-08-02"; :>> judgedBy = "claudeOpus"; }
        #Covers dependency from sittingReview20260802g to wsSupersededGuard;
        // Backlog stub (server WS-hunt LOW / defense-in-depth, issueWsSessionAliveMustChange) — add must_change
        // to session_alive so the per-delivery liveness check is self-contained. NOT started (needs a server
        // redeploy; not exploitable — every must_change path already revokes tokens, which session_alive catches).
        action wsSessionAliveMustCheckBacklog;
        verification wsSessionAliveMustCheckBacklogDoD : Test { :>> id = "a1b2c3d4-1700-4a10-9b20-d1700c0de019"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "Ships with 1.17.0 (server; redeploy). The WS per-delivery liveness re-check (ws.rs session_alive) now also asserts !users.must_change(user) (fail-closed on a poisoned lock), so a must-change account's live socket tears down through the must_change dimension ITSELF — self-contained defense-in-depth, no longer merely transitive through the paired token revocation. Critique: no new deadlock (session_alive holds no lock across the new users lock; no caller holds st.users), no wrongful teardown (normal accounts must_change=false). Guard: ws::tests::ws_session_dies_when_the_account_is_flagged_must_change + clippy. Resolves issueWsSessionAliveMustChange."; }
        part wsSessionAliveMustCheckBacklogDoDR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "a1b2c3d4-1700-4a10-9b20-d1700c0de020"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "b997a63"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-08-05"; :>> judgedBy = "claudeOpus"; }
        // ===== Sprint timestampSettingsUx (2026-08-03) — 1.12.7: declutter the timestamp settings + turn the
        // ignored-date-fields textarea into a validated add/remove list (owner: prevent errors). =====
        action timestampSettingsUx;
        verification timestampSettingsUxDoD : Test { :>> id = "28fb6ca7-5024-4e91-c7b3-16ad04f13ba4"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "Ships PATCH 1.12.7 (UX; client-only, NO server redeploy). Owner-directed: 'revisit the timestamp area UX — descriptions way too verbose, and the date field identification should be an array input, not a huge text field; we try and prevent errors.' FIX (renderIgnoreTimestamps): (1) all three descriptions tightened to one short line; (2) the 'Ignored date fields' 5-row TEXTAREA replaced with a validated ADD-a-row LIST (each key a row + Remove; an 'Add a date field' input + 'Add field' button gated by a new pure validateTimestampKey in frontmatter.ts that rejects empty / ':' / unmatchable / case-insensitive-duplicate keys with a short Notice — errors PREVENTED, not silently accepted); (3) a 'Restore default date fields' safety shown only when the list drifts (the old textarea's implicit empty->defaults, now explicit). No reconcile-semantics change (same s.ignoredTimestampKeys + saveSettings). Guards (fail-first for the validator): frontmatter.test 'validateTimestampKey' (accepts default shapes/wildcards/spaced keys, trims, rejects empty/colon/junk/case-dup); settings-ui.dom 'date fields are a validated add/remove LIST' + 'an INVALID or DUPLICATE date field is REJECTED'. DoD: full client vitest (573) + tsc clean + esbuild build clean + keel validate/guard green. Resolves issueTimestampSettingsVerboseUx."; }
