        // same"); the real fix is to render the collapse header as a real SettingGroup heading. =====
        action collapseHeaderGroupFix;
        verification collapseHeaderGroupFixDoD : Test { :>> id = "8ef1024d-b68a-4f57-1b01-72fc59479b1c"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "Ships PATCH 1.12.10 (UX; client-only, NO server redeploy). Owner-reported on 1.12.9 AFTER a hard restart (so 1.12.9 was running): the '7 synced' collapse still rendered as a small dim row, not a section heading. Cause: 1.12.8/1.12.9 used Setting().setHeading() — an inline heading ROW (.setting-item-heading) — whereas the prominent section headings the owner compares against ('Synced community plugins', 'Advanced') are SettingGroup headings, which mobile themes style far more prominently; no setName()/font-weight tweak could close the gap. FIX: render the collapsible() header as a real new SettingGroup(c).setHeading(title) — the SAME component as the other section headings, so it renders identically on every theme — and toggle the group's PUBLIC listEl (since Obsidian 1.11.0) as the body, rendering rows into it; the native lucide chevron is prepended to the heading, reached via listEl.previousElementSibling (public API, not an internal class name). styles.css: dropped the now-moot .selfsync-collapse-header font-weight override, kept only the chevron affordance. Guard: settings-ui.dom 'the Timestamp changes section is a collapsible ...' updated to find the SettingGroup heading + toggle its listEl (still green). DoD: full client vitest (576) + tsc clean + esbuild build clean + keel validate/guard green. Resolves issueCollapseStillNotHeadingMobile."; }
