        action collapseChevronFix;
        verification collapseChevronFixDoD : Test { :>> id = "a1b2c3d4-1210-4a10-9b20-d1210c0de009"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "Ships PATCH 1.14.1 (UX; client-only, NO server redeploy). Owner-reported on 1.14.0 (mobile screenshot): the '7 synced' SettingGroup heading looked right but its chevron was DETACHED — inside the list card, divorced from the label, and the label didn't toggle. Cause: 1.12.10 placed the chevron/click by GUESSING the heading via group.listEl.previousElementSibling, which is wrong on mobile Obsidian's SettingGroup DOM. FIX: add the chevron with addExtraButton (the documented way to add a control to a SettingGroup heading) so it lands IN the heading next to the label with no DOM guessing; the whole heading row toggles, derived from the button via the stable .setting-item class; graceful degradation (chevron button toggles even if the row-click derivation fails). obsidian-stub models SettingGroup.addExtraButton in the heading. Guard: settings-ui.dom 'the Timestamp changes section is a collapsible ...' still green. DoD: full client vitest (583) + tsc + esbuild build clean + keel validate/guard green. Resolves issueCollapseChevronDetached."; }
