        action connectionRowOverflowFix;
        verification connectionRowOverflowFixDoD : Test { :>> id = "a1b2c3d4-1501-4a10-9b20-d1501c0de013"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "Ships PATCH 1.15.1 (UX; client-only, NO server redeploy). Owner-reported on 1.15.0 (mobile screenshot): the Connection Server row rendered its long https:// URL inline in the control strip with the Setup/Disconnect buttons, pushing Disconnect off the card's right edge on a narrow screen. FIX: factRow renders each fact value as the row DESCRIPTION (full-width, wraps) rather than an inline control-area span, so the control row holds only the action buttons — robust for any long value (long username/vault name too). Retired the unused .selfsync-value CSS. Guard: settings-ui.dom green. DoD: full client vitest (585) + tsc + esbuild build clean + keel validate/guard green. Resolves issueConnectionRowButtonOverflow."; }
        part connectionRowOverflowFixDoDR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "a1b2c3d4-1501-4a10-9b20-d1501c0de014"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "40fab98"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-08-04"; :>> judgedBy = "claudeOpus"; }
        #Covers dependency from sittingReview20260803a to connectionRowOverflowFix;
        // ===== 1.16.0 — per-plugin Push/Pull (replaces the inert direction dropdown; owner-directed). =====
        action pluginPushPull;
        verification pluginPushPullDoD : Test { :>> id = "a1b2c3d4-1600-4a10-9b20-d1600c0de015"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "Ships MINOR 1.16.0 (new capability; client-only, NO server redeploy). Owner-identified quandary: the per-plugin config-sync direction dropdown was INERT for an already-synced plugin (it only governed a no-base first contact) — flipping it did nothing, silently (an nHonestStatus / L-5 gap; issuePluginDirectionInert). Owner chose option #1: replace the dropdown (installed+synced plugin on a read-write vault) with explicit PUSH (make the server + other devices match this device's copy) / PULL (replace this device's copy with the server's) — confirmed authoritative overwrites scoped to .obsidian/plugins/<id>/, over the UNION of local+server files (pluginFilePaths), reusing the tested resolveConfigConflict per path. INDEPENDENT CRITIQUE run on the data-safety: fixed the self-folder guard to the shared case-insensitive+legacy isSelfPluginId (forcePlugin bypasses shouldSync — must not touch SelfSync's credential folder) and made partial-failure reported not swallowed; findings 3-5 (reconcile concurrency = same profile as removePluginFromServer; resolveConfigConflict inner read-only guard; filtered-io.list strand) accepted with rationale. community-plugins.json (enabled list) is never in the union, so Push/Pull can't disable a plugin fleet-wide. Guards: pluginFilePaths (union/scope/no-prefix-bleed) + isSelfPluginId (case-insensitive+legacy) pure tests + settings-ui.dom 'a synced+installed plugin offers Push/Pull ...' wiring test; full client vitest (589) + tsc + esbuild build clean + keel validate/guard green. Resolves issuePluginDirectionInert; realizes nHonestStatus."; }
        part pluginPushPullDoDR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "a1b2c3d4-1600-4a10-9b20-d1600c0de016"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "3079cd7"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-08-04"; :>> judgedBy = "claudeOpus"; }
        #Covers dependency from sittingReview20260803a to pluginPushPull;
        // ===== 1.17.0 — MFA deprecation (D0038): the code disabling MFA behind the mfa_enabled flag. =====
        action mfaDeprecation;
        verification mfaDeprecationDoD : Test { :>> id = "a1b2c3d4-1700-4a10-9b20-d1700c0de021"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "Ships MINOR 1.17.0 (SERVER REDEPLOY). Realizes D0038: MFA (TOTP) disabled behind a runtime mfa_enabled flag (env MFA_ENABLED, default OFF), the mfa.rs/totp.rs code retained. auth::login enforces the TOTP second factor ONLY when mfa_enabled (an already-enrolled account signs in with password alone — no lockout; the password gate is unchanged, so a wrong password still fails); require_admin's REQUIRE_ADMIN_MFA gate applies only when mfa_enabled, with a boot warning if REQUIRE_ADMIN_MFA=1 && !MFA_ENABLED (critique #1 silent-downgrade guard); /api/mfa/* mounted only when enabled; /api/admin/me reports mfa_enabled + the admin console hides the Two-factor panel. Independent critique verdict: safe to ship (no High/Med; no auth bypass; no lockout; no deadlock). Guards: mfa_is_off_by_default (routes 404 + me.mfa_enabled false), the retained mfa_totp_full_lifecycle + require_admin_mfa via for_test_mfa (proving MFA_ENABLED=1 reversal still works), clippy -D warnings, client vitest 589. Realizes D0038; issueMfaLoginUnsupported mooted by D0038."; }
        part mfaDeprecationDoDR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "a1b2c3d4-1700-4a10-9b20-d1700c0de022"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "b997a63"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-08-05"; :>> judgedBy = "claudeOpus"; }
        #Covers dependency from sittingReview20260803a to mfaDeprecation;
        // ===== 1.18.0 — change provenance + source-driven config-change notifications (owner-directed; SERVER REDEPLOY). =====
        action changeProvenanceNotify;
        verification changeProvenanceNotifyDoD : Test { :>> id = "a1b2c3d4-1800-4a10-9b20-d1800c0de023"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "Ships MINOR 1.18.0 (new capability; SERVER REDEPLOY — SQLite index schema v2). Owner-directed: attribute every synced .obsidian/ config/plugin change to WHO made it and notify by SOURCE, retiring the shared-vs-private 'trust the source' warning that fired even on the owner's OWN plugin updates (the noise the owner flagged). SERVER: files-index columns author_user (SERVER-authenticated committer, never a client field), author_device_id, author_device_name; commit(req,&user) records them + changes() returns them; additive serde(default, skip_serializing_if) protocol fields (NO API_VERSION bump); v1->v2 migrate via idempotent ALTER-ADD (pre-provenance rows read None). CLIENT: a STABLE per-device UUID (crypto.randomUUID + WebView-safe non-throwing fallback, minted + DURABLY persisted at load via ensureDeviceId, independent of the mutable device name) stamped on every commit; per-device toggle configChangeNotify = 'user' (default: notify ONLY on ANOTHER PERSON's change) | 'userDevice' (also another of your OWN devices); own edits stay silent; identity = authenticated account then the UUID, so a rename can neither forge nor dodge a notice; the plugin-CODE hot-load-vs-restart RCE barrier is UNCHANGED + orthogonal (still gates on a freshly re-derived vaultIsPrivate). The decision rule is the pure, exhaustively-tested shouldNotifyConfigChange (unknown author -> conservative notify). INDEPENDENT SECURITY CRITIQUE run pre-ship (distinct lenses on spec+diff): FIXED finding-1 HIGH (community-plugins.json union-merge bypassed applyPull so recorded NO provenance -> every plugin enable/disable notified as 'unknown source', re-creating the spam; now records onRemoteConfig), finding-2 (per-surface path scoping so a mixed flush never misattributes one surface's change to another's author), finding-3 (randomUUID WebView fallback, never throws on the connect path), finding-4 (device id durably minted at load, not fire-and-forget), finding-5 (stale provenance cleared each pass); confirmed CLEAN: author is unforgeable (server-set; client CommitRequest carries no author field), the RCE hot-load barrier is intact, migration back-compat is safe, and the notify logic is total. SCOPED OUT (honest limitation, tracked): a peer's config/plugin DELETION is applied WITHOUT a notice because the Deletion wire type carries no provenance -> issueDeletionProvenanceUnnotified, a follow-up. Guards: full server cargo test + clippy -D warnings green; client vitest 603 (new shouldNotifyConfigChange/changeSourceLabel spoof-resistance tests, protocol author-mapping tests, parseSettings coercion, transport device-stamp test, rewritten source-driven CSS wiring test; server v1->v2 migration + commit-provenance tests) + tsc + esbuild build clean; keel validate/guard green. Realizes nChangeAttribution + ucNotifyForeignConfigChange."; }
        part changeProvenanceNotifyDoDR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "a1b2c3d4-1800-4a10-9b20-d1800c0de024"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "7fb0fc9"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-08-05"; :>> judgedBy = "claudeOpus"; }
        #Covers dependency from sittingReview20260803a to changeProvenanceNotify;
        verification sittingReview20260803a : Test { :>> id = "4abd8ec9-7246-4b13-e9d5-38cf26135dc6"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::confirmation; :>> procedureText = "Per-sitting human review (D0049) for the 2026-08-03→05 sitting — a long owner-directed arc of settings-UX cleanup, sharing/onboarding rework, and two capability changes, each shipped as a release the owner iterated on: the timestamp-settings + collapsible-header UX refined against the owner's on-device mobile screenshots (timestampSettingsUx 1.12.7, settingsUxPolish 1.12.8, collapseHeaderFix 1.12.9, collapseHeaderGroupFix 1.12.10, collapseChevronFix 1.14.1); share-links-as-canonical + link onboarding + the admin-console rework (shareLinksCanonical/shareLinkOnboarding 1.13.0, accountCreationLink 1.14.0, D0037) + a test-reliability guard (pluginWiringTimerLeakFix); the mockup-approved settings-tab revamp (settingsRevamp 1.15.0) + its overflow fix (connectionRowOverflowFix 1.15.1); per-plugin Push/Pull replacing the inert direction dropdown (pluginPushPull 1.16.0); MFA deprecation behind a runtime flag (mfaDeprecation 1.17.0, D0038); and the change-provenance + source-driven config-change notifications the owner designed interactively — user+device identity, a stable per-device UUID as the spoof-proof identity, a user-default notify toggle, non-blocking notices, phase-2-first (changeProvenanceNotify 1.18.0). Every behavior/data/security-touching release went through an independent antagonistic critique before ship, which caught + fixed real bugs (e.g. the share-link enumeration oracle, the Push/Pull self-folder guard, and the 1.18.0 community-plugins.json notification-spam gap). The owner SIGNED OFF on 2026-08-05 ('reviewed') — an explicit acceptance of the sitting's completed + released content through 1.18.0. Single human confirmation gate for the sitting; each sprint's closeOut (inspect) + retro (analysis) ran autonomously."; }
        part sittingReview20260803aR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "4abd8ec9-7246-4b13-e9d5-38cf26135dc7"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "2fa1a63"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-08-05"; :>> judgedBy = "wweatherholtz"; }
        // ===== 1.19.0 — Push/Pull preview (owner-directed: "more intelligence on push & pull"). NEW sitting. =====
        action pushPullPreview;
        verification pushPullPreviewDoD : Test { :>> id = "a1b2c3d4-1900-4a10-9b20-d1900c0de025"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "Ships MINOR 1.19.0 (new capability; client-only, NO server redeploy). Owner intent: 'more intelligence on push & pull — what are we pushing to and from?' — the shipped Push/Pull (1.16.0) only showed a generic 'Overwrite the server's copy' confirm, never WHAT it overwrites. FIX: a PREVIEW modal fronting each per-plugin Push/Pull — the direction/ENDPOINTS (this device <-> the server + your other devices), a per-file classification (overwrite / add / remove) + counts, and an on-demand line diff for the changed text settings; an already-in-sync folder shows 'nothing to change' + disables Confirm. New pure pushpreview.ts — classifyPushPull MIRRORS resolveConfigConflict exactly (push: local-absent=>delete server, else overwrite/create; pull: server-absent=>delete here, else overwrite/create), with a presence-vs-hash SideState so an unreadable file classifies per what the real action sees; lineDiff reuses merge.ts's tested LCS anchors (capped 2000 lines). New pushpreviewmodal.ts (lazy per-file diffs). Uses the SAME file union (pluginFilePaths) + hash basis (local sha256 vs server FileMeta.hash — un-normalized config, so comparable) + data source (io.list + changes(0)) as forcePlugin, so the preview cannot disagree with what Push/Pull actually does. INDEPENDENT SECURITY CRITIQUE run pre-ship (distinct lenses on spec+diff): CONFIRMED clean — hash basis, diff direction, self-plugin credential-folder guard (isSelfPluginId returns null before any read; never opens SelfSync's own data.json), modal resolution (only an explicit Confirm resolves true; dismiss=false; no double-resolve), read-only-vault guard (no Push button on a read-only vault + forcePlugin defense-in-depth). FIXED finding-1 MEDIUM (unbounded memory — the preview slurped whole files to hash/diff; now SIZE-GATED: a large file is neither read-to-hash nor fetched-to-diff, matching the real pull's streaming, so no mobile OOM) + finding-3 LOW (an unreadable-but-present local file now classifies per direction — a pull is an overwrite, not a false 'add'). ACCEPTED finding-2 with rationale: the real push re-commits every present file, but the server's IDEMPOTENT commit short-circuit (vault.rs: identical path+hash+chunks => returns the existing meta unchanged — no version bump, no provenance restamp, no broadcast) makes an unchanged re-push a genuine no-op, so the 'unchanged' label is honest about the OUTCOME. Guards: full client vitest 619 (new classifyPushPull + lineDiff pure tests incl. presence/size/unread edge cases + a PushPreviewModal DOM test proving endpoints/summary/lazy-diff/confirm-resolution) + tsc + esbuild build clean; keel validate/guard green. Realizes nPushPullPreview + ucPreviewPushPull."; }
        part pushPullPreviewDoDR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "a1b2c3d4-1900-4a10-9b20-d1900c0de026"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "8daa0bd"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-08-05"; :>> judgedBy = "claudeOpus"; }
        #Covers dependency from sittingReview20260805a to pushPullPreview;
        // ===== 1.20.0 — instant Push/Pull grey-out (hint) + faster on-click check (owner: "lots of inactionable push/pulls"). =====
        action pushPullGreyout;
        verification pushPullGreyoutDoD : Test { :>> id = "a1b2c3d4-2000-4a10-9b20-d2000c0de027"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "Ships MINOR 1.20.0 (client-only, NO server redeploy). Owner feedback on 1.19.0: 'lots of push/pulls that are inactionable — grey them out if the server already holds our changes / the device already has the server's config; but checking is slow (~2s on mobile), I don't want them prechecked all the time. options?' Of three presented options the owner chose INSTANT, network-free grey-out from sync state. FIX: pluginSyncClean(id) decides if a plugin folder is already CONVERGED (local == last-synced base) INSTANTLY + network-free — the pure stampsConverged() compares the base's persisted (size,mtime) stamps to a SCOPED walkConfigTree of just .obsidian/plugins/<id> (NO whole-vault io.list, NO changes(0) server fetch, NO hashing); conservative on ANY doubt (recorded config conflict, missing stamp, set mismatch, unlistable folder) → NOT converged. Settings DIMS Push/Pull as a hint when converged (cached for instant no-flicker re-render + refreshed async each render; entry dropped after a push/pull, cache cleared on hide). PERF: the on-click preview now also scopes its local list to the plugin folder (was the whole-vault io.list — the owner-reported ~2s). INDEPENDENT SECURITY CRITIQUE run pre-ship: confirmed conservative-toward-live everywhere that matters, scoped-walk equivalence for the rendered case, guard robustness, no uncaught exception paths. FIXED its one MEDIUM finding (§1): the grey-out shares auto-sync's (size,mtime) skip heuristic, so an out-of-band change preserving BOTH size AND mtime is invisible to auto-sync — and a HARD-disabled override would then trap the user (couldn't Pull to restore a locally-corrupted file). Fix per the critique's recommendation: the grey-out is a HINT, never a lock — buttons stay CLICKABLE (dimmed via opacity, NOT setDisabled), and a click ALWAYS runs the accurate preview, so the manual override can always recover the truth. Guards: full client vitest 625 (new stampsConverged pure tests incl. stamp-drift / set-mismatch / no-stamp edge cases + a settings DOM test proving the buttons DIM yet stay clickable + run the accurate preview) + tsc + esbuild build clean; keel validate/guard green. Realizes nPushPullPreview (viability visibility + performance)."; }
        part pushPullGreyoutDoDR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "a1b2c3d4-2000-4a10-9b20-d2000c0de028"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "0fc2f78"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-08-05"; :>> judgedBy = "claudeOpus"; }
        #Covers dependency from sittingReview20260805a to pushPullGreyout;
        // ===== 1.21.0 — author + timestamp in the Push/Pull preview (owner: "know the author + a timestamp"). =====
        action pushPullProvenance;
        verification pushPullProvenanceDoD : Test { :>> id = "a1b2c3d4-2100-4a10-9b20-d2100c0de029"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "Ships MINOR 1.21.0 (client-only, NO server redeploy). Owner: 'I want to know the author when I'm pushing and overwriting settings, and when pulling settings. I want a timestamp and a user' — the original 'made from Wills Desktop at X timestamp' format they'd described. The 1.18.0 change-provenance (author + device_id/name + mtime) already rides on every server FileMeta and pluginPushPullPreview already fetches it via changes(0); this SURFACES it in the preview. Each preview row that touches a SERVER copy now shows 'on server: <user> · <device> · <when>' — a Push tells you WHOSE settings you're overwriting/removing, a Pull tells you whose you're adopting. A local-only file (no server copy) shows no line; a pre-1.18.0 file (no author recorded) shows just the timestamp. author is SERVER-AUTHENTICATED (unspoofable); deviceName is a display-only label. Pure FileChangeView + serverProvenanceWho() helper; the modal formats mtime (toLocaleString). Display-only — no sync behavior/data change, no server change — so a SELF-REVIEW stands in for a full independent critique (setText escapes any label; the provenance is already-validated FileMeta data; author can't be spoofed). Guards: full client vitest 629 (serverProvenanceWho pure test + a modal DOM test asserting the who/device line renders on the overwrite + delete rows, and is absent on a local-only create) + tsc + esbuild build clean; keel validate/guard green. Realizes nChangeAttribution + nPushPullPreview (completing the owner's original 'who + when' intent in the push/pull path)."; }
        part pushPullProvenanceDoDR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "a1b2c3d4-2100-4a10-9b20-d2100c0de030"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "6da17b6"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-08-05"; :>> judgedBy = "claudeOpus"; }
        #Covers dependency from sittingReview20260805a to pushPullProvenance;
        // ===== 1.21.1 — settings scroll no longer jumps to top on a toggle (owner-reported bug). =====
        action settingsScrollPreserve;
        verification settingsScrollPreserveDoD : Test { :>> id = "a1b2c3d4-2101-4a10-9b20-d2101c0de031"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "Ships PATCH 1.21.1 (bugfix; client-only, NO server redeploy). Owner-reported: 'most of the time when I click an option, a slide toggle on community plugins for example, it resets the settings page to the top.' Root cause: the config-sync surface toggles + the community-plugin checklist call this.display(), which does containerEl.empty() + a full tab rebuild — discarding the scroll position. FIX: display() now captures the scrolling ancestor's scrollTop BEFORE empty() (scrollEl() walks up to the overflow:auto/scroll ancestor) and restores it after the rebuild; sections rebuild at the same heights so the user stays put. Centralised in display() — the single re-render choke point — so EVERY handler that re-renders is fixed structurally, not by per-handler vigilance (D0047: the centralisation IS the durable control; happy-dom has no layout so real scroll isn't unit-testable). Guards: full client vitest 629 (settings-ui.dom still green through the display() restructure — body moved under `if (configured)`) + tsc + esbuild build clean; keel validate/guard green. Resolves issueSettingsScrollResetsOnToggle."; }
        part settingsScrollPreserveDoDR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "a1b2c3d4-2101-4a10-9b20-d2101c0de032"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "23e009b"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-08-05"; :>> judgedBy = "claudeOpus"; }
        #Covers dependency from sittingReview20260805a to settingsScrollPreserve;
        // ===== 1.21.2 — HARD-disable Push/Pull when inactionable (owner reversed the §1 hint). =====
        action pushPullDisableInactionable;
        verification pushPullDisableInactionableDoD : Test { :>> id = "a1b2c3d4-2102-4a10-9b20-d2102c0de033"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "Ships PATCH 1.21.2 (owner-directed behavior change; client-only, NO server redeploy). Owner directed: 'disable push and pull buttons if there is no real action. They're updated quickly enough that if I really want to push, and someone is legitimately updating concurrently, I can wait a second. In the meantime, we'll accurately prevent misleading the user 99%+ of the time.' This REVERSES the pushPullGreyout §1 'hint, not lock' softening (which had kept the buttons dimmed-but-clickable so an out-of-band divergence stayed recoverable). OWNER'S INFORMED ACCEPTANCE of the tradeoff (recorded after I re-surfaced the residual): when the plugin folder is converged (pluginSyncClean), the Push/Pull buttons are now setDisabled AND the act() click is guarded (a no-op) — so a LIVE button ALWAYS means a real overwrite (never misleading). The concurrent-remote-edit case self-heals within ~a second (next poll) — the owner's 'wait a second' reasoning; the ONLY non-self-healing residual — an out-of-band change preserving BOTH size AND mtime — is an accepted, PRE-EXISTING auto-sync blindspot (auto-sync misses it too via the same (size,mtime) skip, so the button was never a reliable recovery for it), acknowledged by the owner. Guards: full client vitest 629 (settings-ui.dom updated: a converged button is DISABLED + its click is a guarded no-op — no preview, no overwrite) + tsc + esbuild build clean; keel validate/guard green. Refines pushPullGreyout (nPushPullPreview); the owner decision + accepted residual are recorded HERE (capture-the-decision, D-invariant §2.4)."; }
        part pushPullDisableInactionableDoDR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "a1b2c3d4-2102-4a10-9b20-d2102c0de034"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "3dffae6"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-08-05"; :>> judgedBy = "claudeOpus"; }
        #Covers dependency from sittingReview20260805a to pushPullDisableInactionable;
        // ===== 1.21.3 — make the disabled Push/Pull buttons genuinely unclickable (owner-reported on 1.21.2). =====
        action pushPullDisableInert;
        verification pushPullDisableInertDoD : Test { :>> id = "a1b2c3d4-2103-4a10-9b20-d2103c0de035"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "Ships PATCH 1.21.3 (bugfix; client-only, NO server redeploy). Owner-reported on 1.21.2: 'the push and pull buttons are grayed, but clickable. they should be disabled/unclickable.' Root cause: ExtraButtonComponent.setDisabled only adds an is-disabled CLASS to the button's div/anchor (not a native <button disabled>), so it GREYS the control but does NOT block the onClick — the act() guard no-op'd the action, but the button still felt interactive. FIX: when converged, also set pointer-events:none on the button element, making it genuinely INERT (no click/hover) — a real disabled control; the act() guard stays as defense-in-depth. GUARD (D0047 — a correction gets a permanent automated guard): the settings-ui.dom test now asserts the converged button's style.pointerEvents === 'none' (not just that a click no-ops), catching any regression to greyed-but-clickable. Guards: full client vitest 629 + tsc + esbuild build clean; keel validate/guard green. Resolves issuePushPullDisabledStillClickable; completes pushPullDisableInactionable."; }
        part pushPullDisableInertDoDR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "a1b2c3d4-2103-4a10-9b20-d2103c0de036"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "466aa82"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-08-05"; :>> judgedBy = "claudeOpus"; }
        #Covers dependency from sittingReview20260805a to pushPullDisableInert;
        verification sittingReview20260805a : Test { :>> id = "5b0d8f05-0805-4a10-9b20-a1b2c3d40805"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::confirmation; :>> procedureText = "Per-sitting human review (D0049) for the 2026-08-05 sitting — the NEW work AFTER the 2026-08-03 sitting was signed off ('reviewed'). The owner reported that pushing plugin settings gave no indication of what it overwrites ('am I forgetting something'), directed 'more intelligence on push & pull — what are we pushing to and from?' + 'record as need please', then followed up that many push/pulls are inactionable and should grey out (but the check is slow on mobile). This gate covers pushPullPreview (1.19.0 — the per-file PREVIEW modal: direction/endpoints + overwrite/add/remove counts + on-demand text diffs), pushPullGreyout (1.20.0 — the instant network-free grey-out HINT + the scoped-list perf fix), and pushPullProvenance (1.21.0 — the SERVER copy's author + device + timestamp per preview row, the owner's original 'who + when' format), the first two built through independent security critiques (preview-matches-action + memory bounds; and the grey-out-is-a-hint-not-a-lock fix), the last a display-only self-reviewed increment. The owner SIGNED OFF on 2026-08-07, directing 'stamp and proceed' — an explicit acceptance of the sitting's released content (1.19.0 through 1.21.3: the Push/Pull preview, the instant grey-out + scoped-list perf fix, the per-row server provenance, the settings-scroll-preserve fix, and the Push/Pull hard-disable + inert-button corrections). Single human confirmation gate for the sitting; each sprint's closeOut (inspect) + retro (analysis) ran autonomously."; }
        part sittingReview20260805aR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "5b0d8f05-0805-4a10-9b20-a1b2c3d40806"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "e0f378e"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-08-07"; :>> judgedBy = "wweatherholtz"; }
        // ===== 1.22.0 — plugin-sync autopilot + peer-approval gate (owner-directed set-and-forget). NEW sitting. =====
        action pluginSyncAutopilot;
        verification pluginSyncAutopilotDoD : Test { :>> id = "a1b2c3d4-2200-4a10-9b20-d2200c0de037"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "Ships MINOR 1.22.0 (new capability + settings-UX; client-only, NO server redeploy). Owner-directed SET-AND-FORGET after a design discussion working through config-sync AUDIENCES (device-local / personal / shared): a 'Auto-sync new plugins' setting (default OFF — auto-propagating plugin CODE is security-sensitive, so opt-in). When on, runPluginAutopilot (on each full reconcile via onRemotePlugins + on settings render): (a) a plugin installed HERE and (b) a server plugin from YOUR OWN account (main.js committer == you, or unknown-author on your PROVABLY-PRIVATE vault) → auto-added to the synced allowlist (upload / adopt); (c) a plugin added by ANOTHER PERSON → NEVER auto-adopted — it lands in a persistent 'Awaiting your approval' list (the reframed Available section, labeled WHO added it) + a one-time toast. Ownership keys on the AUTHENTICATED committer of main.js (the EXECUTABLE), so a device rename can't fake it. A persisted 'seen' set means an un-ticked plugin is never re-added (the policy never fights a manual choice). Bundled settings-UX: copy fixes (plugin rows say what+when — 'here only — uploads to the server on next sync'), removed the redundant 'Sync none' button, and the 'Greyed Push/Pull = already in sync' note. INDEPENDENT SECURITY CRITIQUE run pre-ship: CONFIRMED author is server-authenticated (a peer can't forge author==you) + the autopilot only whitelists/downloads — the separate hot-load gate still re-derives vault privacy + keeps the restart/trust barrier, so it CANNOT run a peer's code. FIXED findings: F2 (ownership keys on main.js not manifest.json — a peer overwriting main.js can't be auto-adopted as yours), F1 (author sourced from the reconcile's own manifest — no per-plugin/per-render fileMeta network storm), F4 (peer plugins not marked seen → a later ownership flip can still auto-adopt), F7 (.catch on the fire-and-forget); CONFIRMED clean: F3 (no peer-code execution), F5 (username exact-match, fail-safe). ACCEPTED F6 (documented, = the nPerUserConfigScope SPIKE): on a shared vault, auto-synced plugins land in the shared store visible to peers — personal-vs-shared scope is the pinned spike. Guards: full client vitest 633 (autopilot own-adopt vs peer-gate, un-tick-sticks, off-is-no-op; parseSettings opt-in; reconcile onRemotePlugins carries main.js authors) + tsc + esbuild build clean; keel validate/guard green. Realizes nPluginSyncAutopilot + ucSetAndForgetPluginSync."; }
        part pluginSyncAutopilotDoDR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "a1b2c3d4-2200-4a10-9b20-d2200c0de038"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "e61df7e"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-08-07"; :>> judgedBy = "claudeOpus"; }
        #Covers dependency from sittingReview20260807a to pluginSyncAutopilot;
        // ===== composed-vaults Phase 1 — mount data model + two-sided path math + boundary rules (D0039). NO release. =====
        action mountsFoundation;
        verification mountsFoundationDoD : Test { :>> id = "a1b2c3d4-3900-4a10-9b20-d3900c0de039"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "Phase 1 of the D0039 composed-vaults epic — FOUNDATION only. NO version bump / NO release (internal scaffolding — no engine wiring, no user-facing behavior yet), so CI validates on push but the release/publish workflow does not fire. New PURE module client/src/mounts.ts (no Obsidian API, no engine dependency, so exhaustively unit-testable + can never drift from the reconcile that consumes it in Phase 2+): the Mount type ({source:{owner,vaultId,sourcePath}, mountPoint, direction:'pull'|'sync'}); normFolder (the single source of truth for path comparison/building); the LOAD-BEARING BOUNDARY rules claimsLocal / primaryExcludes (segment-safe — a sibling that merely shares a name prefix is NOT claimed — so the primary reconcile scope excludes exactly the mount points and a mounted file never double-syncs to the primary server vault, the one invariant a bug here would corrupt/duplicate data); the two-sided path translation local <-> mount-relative <-> source-S-relative (mountRelFromLocal / mountRelFromSource / localFromMountRel / sourceFromMountRel, whole-source vs subfolder, round-trip); validateMounts (rejects empty/root + duplicate + nested mount points, allows name-prefix siblings); and parseMounts (parse-don't-validate at the persistence boundary — drops malformed entries, normalizes both paths, defaults an unknown direction to the SAFE 'pull'). Plus the settings.mounts PER-DEVICE data model (composition is a local choice, never synced — like the primary target; normalized + malformed-dropped on parse). Guards: full client vitest 648 (new client/test/mounts.test.ts — normFolder, boundary + segment-safety, two-sided round-trip, whole-source vs subfolder, validateMounts overlap/nest, parseMounts coercion/drop) + tsc --noEmit clean; keel validate/guard green. Realizes nComposedVaults (Phase 1 of N — foundation). Next: Phase 2 (pull mount engine + MountedIo adapter + per-mount FSM + aggregate status fold)."; }
        part mountsFoundationDoDR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "a1b2c3d4-3900-4a10-9b20-d3900c0de040"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "2933ee7"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-08-07"; :>> judgedBy = "claudeOpus"; }
        #Covers dependency from sittingReview20260807a to mountsFoundation;
        verification sittingReview20260807a : Test { :>> id = "7a0d8f07-0807-4a10-9b20-a1b2c3d40807"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::confirmation; :>> procedureText = "Per-sitting human review (D0049) for the 2026-08-07 sitting. After a design discussion (the owner worked through config-sync AUDIENCES — device-local / personal / shared — confirmed they DO share vaults with others, and pinned two SPIKES: nPerUserConfigScope + nComposedVaults for a later brainstorm), the owner directed 'do the shared vault feature now': the plugin-sync AUTOPILOT (pluginSyncAutopilot, 1.22.0) — set-and-forget auto-sync of your own new plugins with a peer-approval gate keyed on the authenticated main.js committer — plus the bundled settings-UX (copy fixes, 'Sync none' removed, the 'Greyed = already in sync' note). Built through an independent security critique (main.js-not-manifest ownership + no fetch-storm fixes). The owner SIGNED OFF on 2026-08-07, directing 'stamp and proceed' — an explicit acceptance of the sitting's content: the plugin-sync autopilot + bundled settings-UX (1.22.0) and the composed-vaults Phase 1 foundation (mountsFoundation — internal scaffolding, method=test self-evidencing). Single human confirmation gate for the sitting; each sprint's closeOut (inspect) + retro (analysis) ran autonomously."; }
        part sittingReview20260807aR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "7a0d8f07-0807-4a10-9b20-a1b2c3d40808"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "e0f378e"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-08-07"; :>> judgedBy = "wweatherholtz"; }
        // ===== composed-vaults Phase 2 (1/n) — MountedIo + MountedApi prefix-translating adapters (D0039). NEW sitting. NO release. =====
        action mountIoAdapters;
        verification mountIoAdaptersDoD : Test { :>> id = "a1b2c3d4-3901-4a10-9b20-d3901c0de041"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "Phase 2 (increment 1) of the D0039 composed-vaults epic — the two-sided PREFIX-TRANSLATING adapters that let a Mount reuse the existing reconcile engine unchanged. ENGINE-INTERNAL (not yet wired to a live reconcile), NO version bump / NO release. New PURE module client/src/mountio.ts (no Obsidian API, no transport — wraps an injected VaultIo/SyncApi, so exhaustively unit-testable): MountedIo (local-side mount-relative <-> <mountPoint>/<rel>; list() exposes ONLY the mount subtree, re-keyed + data-only-filtered; exists/appendWrite mirror the base's capability); MountedApi (source-side mount-relative <-> <sourcePath>/<rel> over a source-vault-bound API; changes() drops outside-subtree + config paths but preserves the source-global version so the cursor stays consistent; HARD-REFUSES commit/deleteFile on a pull/read-only mount — the load-bearing safety net); isDataPath (the data-only boundary, reject .obsidian/**, case-folded). INDEPENDENT SECURITY CRITIQUE run pre-commit (3 lenses: path-translation, invariant-bypass, reconcile-integration). FIXED: B1 HIGH (deleteFile guarded read-only but NOT data-only — a sync mount could delete source config; now symmetric with commit), A1 MED (normFolder trimmed each segment, corrupting round-trip for a filename with legitimate leading/trailing whitespace — now round-trip-faithful; user-input trim deferred to the Phase-4 UI), B2 MED (fileMeta returns null for a config path — config invisible even via a direct lookup), B3 (isDataPath case-folded so .Obsidian can't bypass on a case-insensitive FS). CONFIRMED CLEAN: read-only structurally sound (B4); the delete-guard ratio uses the mount's FILTERED manifest, not the global version (C2); the filtered stream manufactures no phantom deletions + the cursor stays in source-global space (C3). RECORDED as a tracked hazard (issueMountBaseIsolation, C1 HIGH — NOT adapter-enforceable): the Phase-3 wiring MUST give each mount its OWN base+state (a shared base -> phantom mass-delete), marked by a load-bearing invariant comment + resolved by the mountEngine action. ACCEPTED C4 LOW (a legitimately-emptied small mount subtree trips the conservative bulk-delete guard — a Phase-3 delete-propagation concern, no corruption). Guards: full client vitest 661 (mountio.test — local/source translation, whole-source, capability mirror, read-only refusal, symmetric config write/delete refusal, fileMeta config-null, case-fold; mounts.test — whitespace round-trip) + tsc --noEmit clean; keel validate/guard green. Realizes nComposedVaults (Phase 2 adapters)."; }
        part mountIoAdaptersDoDR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "a1b2c3d4-3901-4a10-9b20-d3901c0de042"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "58c2fdd"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-08-07"; :>> judgedBy = "claudeOpus"; }
        #Covers dependency from sittingReview20260807b to mountIoAdapters;
        // ===== composed-vaults Phase 2 (2/n) — the pure mount-engine CORE (per-mount runtime + FSM + status fold). NO release. =====
        action mountEngineCore;
        verification mountEngineCoreDoD : Test { :>> id = "a1b2c3d4-3902-4a10-9b20-d3902c0de043"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "Phase 2 (increment 2) of the D0039 composed-vaults epic — the pure mount-engine core that lets a mount run as a SECOND concurrent reconcile scope reusing the pure engine unchanged. ENGINE-INTERNAL (not yet driven by a live loop), NO version bump / NO release. Two pure modules (no Obsidian API, no transport — unit-testable): (1) mountengine.ts — MountRuntime bundles one mount's scope and STRUCTURALLY owns its isolation: it ALWAYS constructs its OWN BaseStore + SyncState + DeleteRateGuard + retry budget, so a caller CANNOT inject the primary's — making issueMountBaseIsolation (critique C1 HIGH: a shared base -> phantom mass-delete) impossible to violate by construction; deps() assembles a ReconcileDeps over the mount's own base/state + the MountedIo/MountedApi wrappers + the isDataPath data-only accepts, with readOnly=true for a PULL mount (reconcile's pull-only path, defense-in-depth with MountedApi's write hard-refuse); mountKey() is a stable order-independent per-mount identity for persisting its own base+cursor (MountPersist). (2) mountfsm.ts — the per-mount lifecycle FSM (detached/mounting/live/syncing/diverged/offline/unmounting/failed) as a pure transition (unmount+fail from any live state; unknown transition = conservative no-op), plus the aggregate status FOLD (mountHealth/foldHealth/aggregateStatus) that folds the primary scope's health with every mount's and surfaces the WORST as the single status light's state + reason, so a struggling mount is never masked (nor masks the primary). Same pure-projection discipline as connstate/transportstate/statuslight. Guards: full client vitest 673 (mountengine.test — structural isolation [distinct base/state/guard per runtime + mutation isolation], restore/persist round-trip, deps wiring, pull=readOnly; FSM happy-path + offline/diverged/failed recovery + unmount/fail-from-any + no-op; fold worst-wins + reason) + tsc --noEmit clean; keel validate/guard green. Resolves the ISOLATION invariant of issueMountBaseIsolation STRUCTURALLY (the live mountEngine wiring will still assert it end-to-end before the issue closes). Realizes nComposedVaults (Phase 2 engine core)."; }
        part mountEngineCoreDoDR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "a1b2c3d4-3902-4a10-9b20-d3902c0de044"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "cb36a8e"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-08-07"; :>> judgedBy = "claudeOpus"; }
        #Covers dependency from sittingReview20260807b to mountEngineCore;
        // ===== composed-vaults Phase 3 (1/n + 2/n) — the LIVE mount engine (sync loop + main.ts wiring). Resolver for issueMountBaseIsolation. NO release (dormant). =====
        action mountEngine;
        verification mountEngineDoD : Test { :>> id = "a1b2c3d4-3903-4a10-9b20-d3903c0de045"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "Phase 3 of the D0039 composed-vaults epic — the LIVE mount engine, wired into the plugin as a SECOND concurrent sync scope per settings.mounts entry, DORMANT until a mount is configured (no UI sets one yet → zero behaviour change; NO version bump / NO release). Two increments: (1) mountsync.ts — the sync LOOP (pollMount → decideReconcileMode → reconcileAll|reconcileDelta; reconcileMountScope(s) advancing the pure mountfsm, fail-isolated: a poll throw → offline (transient) or failed after MAX_MOUNT_FAILS), exercised END-TO-END in unit tests over the REAL reconcile engine (faithful chunked source + in-memory io); (2) main.ts glue — mountScopes/mountStateStore/sessionToken/mountIo fields, buildMountApi (a HttpTransport bound to the SOURCE vault, same server+session token), rebuildMountScopes (build/preserve/dedupe/restore-own-base+cursor), reconcileMounts (DETACHED + re-entrancy-guarded + fail-isolated, run after the primary pass), the primary-scope BOUNDARY exclusion (activeMounts() feeds both passes/accepts AND scope-building), mountState persistence, teardown cleanup. v1 is POLL-DRIVEN on the primary cycle (per-mount real-time ws deferred, D0040). INDEPENDENT SECURITY CRITIQUE (3 lenses) + a re-verify pass, both pre-commit. FIXED: A1 HIGH (the mount had reused the primary's filtered io → mount writes silently dropped + a reconnect delete-remote'd the SOURCE vault; now a mount wraps a separate DATA-ONLY io — forMount: passes=!isConfigPath, no mount-exclusion, no .obsidian walk — the traversal-safety guard stays); A2/C3 MED (a hand-edited overlapping/duplicate mount set is rejected wholesale via validateMounts + deduped by mountKey); B1 MED (reconcileMounts DETACHED + re-entrancy-guarded so a hung mount can't stall the primary engine queue); B2/N2 MED/LOW (mountState loaded via a validated parseMountState — finite ≥0 version, base entries need a string hash, non-string merge-ancestor text dropped — so hostile persisted input can't reach the engine); N1 MED (the primary exclusion + scope-building now share ONE activeMounts() validated set, so a bad set can't leave a folder excluded-from-primary yet handled-by-no-mount). CONFIRMED CLEAN + re-confirmed after fixes: pull=read-only (deps.readOnly + MountedApi hard-refuse + reconcile readOnly throw), throw fail-isolation, per-mount base/state/guard isolation (each MountRuntime constructs its OWN — a caller cannot inject the primary's), persist single-flight coalescing of base+mountState, content-addressed cache sharing. ACCEPTED N3 LOW (a never-settling source poll leaves the subsystem dormant — not reachable via HttpTransport's request timeout; strictly better than hanging the primary). HONEST RESIDUAL: no end-to-end integration test through the REAL Obsidian ObsidianVaultIo (not unit-testable without Obsidian) — validated by the critique's static trace + the owner's on-device pass (Phase 4). Guards: full client vitest 683 (mountsync end-to-end pull/push/fail-isolation/recovery; parseMountState hostile-input validation) + tsc --noEmit clean + esbuild build clean; keel validate/guard green. RESOLVES issueMountBaseIsolation (isolation structurally enforced + critique-re-confirmed). Realizes nComposedVaults (Phase 3 live engine, dormant)."; }
        part mountEngineDoDR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "a1b2c3d4-3903-4a10-9b20-d3903c0de046"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "13fbd86"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-08-07"; :>> judgedBy = "claudeOpus"; }
        #Covers dependency from sittingReview20260807b to mountEngine;
        // ===== composed-vaults Phase 4 — the mount-management UX (settings section + guided add modal). NO release (staged for an on-device pass). =====
        action mountUx;
        verification mountUxDoD : Test { :>> id = "a1b2c3d4-3904-4a10-9b20-d3904c0de047"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "Phase 4 of the D0039 composed-vaults epic — the user-facing UX, the FIRST consumer that lets a mount be configured (activating the otherwise-dormant engine). Built from a use-case + human-factors analysis (the driver is the safety of a data-moving feature). NO version bump / NO release — the whole composed-vaults feature (Phases 1-4) stays STAGED on main until the owner's on-device pass, then the v1 release. New client/src/mountsettings.ts (pure helpers + the modal): sourceOptions (candidate sources = vaults I own + vaults shared TO me, EXCLUDING the primary so you can't mount a vault into itself, marking write permission), mountRowLabel/mountStateLabel, validateMountDraft (why Save is disabled), and MountEditModal — the guided add form: default PULL (safe, source untouched); SYNC offered ONLY for a writable source and behind a ⚠ warning naming the target + audience; live validation disables Save on overlap/blank/root. settings.ts renderComposedVaults: a collapsed 'Composed vaults' section listing each mount (source→local, direction, live per-mount state) with a NON-DESTRUCTIVE remove flow (files kept as normal notes; the destructive delete option deferred as the safest v1 choice). main.ts: mountStates/addMount/removeMount wiring. INDEPENDENT UX + code CRITIQUE (2 lenses) run pre-commit — headline CONFIRMED: no normal-UI path causes an accidental write/delete to an unintended source (sync is opt-in + write-perm-gated + warned + names the target). FIXED: C1 MED (removeMount raced an in-flight reconcile → the removed mount's state got re-persisted; onEvent now skips a scope no longer in mountScopes), U1 MED (perm not re-checked at save → a save-time downgrade to pull on a non-writable source, defense-in-depth over the trusted-server 403 — D0007), U2/U3 MED (clearer copy: adding DETACHES the folder from primary sync + conflict-copy semantics; removing UPLOADS the kept files to the primary vault + other devices), C4 LOW (saved set only after addMount resolves). ACCEPTED C2 LOW (owner-alias exact-match — not reachable with current transport). Guards: full client vitest 692 (mountsettings pure-helper tests: sourceOptions primary-exclusion + read/readWrite perm, validateMountDraft overlap/root/blank, labels; settings-ui.dom: the section lists a mount with direction+state + Add button, + the empty state) + tsc --noEmit clean + esbuild build clean; keel validate/guard green. Realizes nComposedVaults (Phase 4 UX). REMAINING before v1: the owner's on-device pass, then the release."; }
        part mountUxDoDR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "a1b2c3d4-3904-4a10-9b20-d3904c0de048"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "69857e3"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-08-08"; :>> judgedBy = "claudeOpus"; }
        #Covers dependency from sittingReview20260807b to mountUx;
        // ===== composed-vaults hardening sweep (owner-directed: "5 more rounds of critique, diligently implement one after the other"). NO release. =====
        action mountHardeningR1;
        verification mountHardeningR1DoD : Test { :>> id = "a1b2c3d4-3905-4a10-9b20-d3905c0de049"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "Hardening Round 1 (independent critique, lens: CONCURRENCY & LIFECYCLE races). ENGINE-INTERNAL, NO release. FIXED: F1/F5 MED — an add/reconnect during an in-flight detached mount pass was DROPPED by the re-entrancy guard and never rebuilt (rebuild only fired on initial||empty), so a new mount silently never started AND its folder — already excluded from the primary scope — synced to NOBODY; fix: rebuild EVERY pass (preserve-by-key + add/drop to match the configured set) + defer a mid-pass request (mountReconcilePending) and re-run on release. F2 MED — mount source transports capture the session token by value; a reactive-401 relogin rotated it but the old scope was preserved → 401 forever; fix: track mountScopesToken, drop+rebuild all scopes on rotation (base+cursor survive in mountStateStore → resume). F3 MED (data-touching) — an in-flight pass could mutate the DISK for a just-removed mount before the onEvent guard; fix: removeMount marks the scope 'unmounting' first + reconcileMountScopes re-checks an isLive predicate before driving each scope. F4 LOW-MED — a detached pass could write to the vault after teardown/unload; fix: isLive returns false when unloading + the deferred re-run is suppressed while unloading. CONFIRMED SAFE: the guard can't stick, no two-pass overlap, persist single-flight coalescing, cache sharing, MountRuntime isolation. Guards: full client vitest 693 (new mountsync isLive-skip test) + tsc + build clean; keel validate/guard green."; }
        part mountHardeningR1DoDR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "a1b2c3d4-3905-4a10-9b20-d3905c0de050"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "dcd13d0"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-08-08"; :>> judgedBy = "claudeOpus"; }
        #Covers dependency from sittingReview20260807b to mountHardeningR1;
        action mountHardeningR2;
        verification mountHardeningR2DoD : Test { :>> id = "a1b2c3d4-3906-4a10-9b20-d3906c0de051"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "Hardening Round 2 (independent critique, lens: DATA INTEGRITY & CORRUPTION). ENGINE-INTERNAL, NO release. FIXED: F1 HIGH (silent data loss) — a PULL mount's first-contact over a pre-existing DIFFERENT local file called adoptRemote with NO conflict copy (readOnly took the fresh-share adopt-over-local path), destroying the user's version — and composing a pull mount over a populated folder is the primary use case; fix: opt-in ReconcileDeps.preserveLocalFirstContact (default OFF → a fresh read-only SHARE + the primary unchanged), mounts set it → a no-base first-contact divergence takes readOnlyKeepCopy (keep the local as a conflict copy + adopt the source, push nothing). F2 MED — the emptyManifest bulk-delete guard is a whole-vault index-loss heuristic that on a legitimately-emptied source SUBTREE refuses forever and was SILENT (onGuard unwired); fix: wire onGuard (toast+log) so the stall is visible, keep the fail-safe (also protects the mount from a source index-loss wipe). F3 MED — the mount hardcoded reset:false + left onKeptAbsent unwired so a SYNC mount could SILENTLY resurrect a peer's deletion into the shared source; fix: wire onKeptAbsent (toast+log) so a keep/restore is visible (a PULL mount can't resurrect — read-only); full D0019 reset-detection for mounts is the tracked follow-up issueMountResetDetection. CONFIRMED CORRECT: base/cursor persist atomically, cursor never skips an in-subtree change, per-mount isolation, removeMount/addMount handoff non-destructive, merge ancestor sound under re-keyed paths. Guards: full client vitest 695 (planMerge firstContactKeepCopy case + a new end-to-end pull-mount-over-existing-file conflict-copy test; full reconcile suite 169 green — the shared flag is opt-in/default-off) + tsc + build clean; keel validate/guard green. Realizes nComposedVaults (hardening)."; }
        part mountHardeningR2DoDR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "a1b2c3d4-3906-4a10-9b20-d3906c0de052"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "8ac8975"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-08-08"; :>> judgedBy = "claudeOpus"; }
        #Covers dependency from sittingReview20260807b to mountHardeningR2;
        action mountHardeningR3;
        verification mountHardeningR3DoD : Test { :>> id = "a1b2c3d4-3907-4a10-9b20-d3907c0de053"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "Hardening Round 3 (independent critique, lens: BOUNDARY & PATH-TRANSLATION adversarial). ENGINE-INTERNAL, NO release. A coherent hardening pass on the pure path/validation layer. FIXED: H1 HIGH — the boundary compare (claimsLocal/mountRelFromLocal/mountRelFromSource/validateMounts) was case-sensitive, so on a case-insensitive FS a case-drifted folder LEAKED to the primary vault while the mount synced nothing (split-brain); fix: segment-based NFC + case-FOLDED matching (matching the codebase's isDataPath/shouldSync convention), rel keeps REAL case for round-trip — also fixes M4 (Unicode NFC/NFD) + M5 (two mounts over one folder by case). H2 HIGH — a mount anchored under .obsidian could pull another vault's config as data or EXFILTRATE SelfSync's credential data.json to the source (read→push); fix: validateMounts REJECTS any mount point or source subfolder inside .obsidian (→ activeMounts empty → dormant + Save disabled) AND ObsidianVaultIo.read/exists refuse a config path on a mount io (defense-in-depth closing the read→push vector). M1 MED — mountKey delimiter-joined form could collide two distinct mounts whose fields contain #/=/> (a folder named 'C#') onto one key → shared base/cursor; fix: JSON-encode the components (collision-free). M3/L2 — a mount point with stray whitespace / trailing dot / backslashes persisted verbatim → inert mount + leak; fix: new normMountFolder sanitizes user config at the parse boundary + the modal draft. L1 — normFolder now drops '..' (defense-in-depth over asSafeVaultPath). CONFIRMED SAFE: segment-boundary safety (ASIx≠ASI), trailing-slash mount point, whole-source .obsidian exclusion both directions, activeMounts() at every primary sink incl. switchTo + config reconcile, activeMounts fail-safe, pull read-only, .obsidianX false-positive. ACCEPTED L3 (duplicate-source-to-multiple-locals — a valid pattern, not blocked). Guards: full client vitest 702 (new adversarial mounts tests: case-insensitive boundary, NFC/NFD, case-dupe reject, .obsidian mount/source reject, normMountFolder sanitize, normFolder .. drop; mountKey non-collision) + tsc + build clean; keel validate/guard green. Realizes nComposedVaults (hardening)."; }
        part mountHardeningR3DoDR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "a1b2c3d4-3907-4a10-9b20-d3907c0de054"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "bb5c0c6"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-08-08"; :>> judgedBy = "claudeOpus"; }
        #Covers dependency from sittingReview20260807b to mountHardeningR3;
        action mountHardeningR4;
        verification mountHardeningR4DoD : Test { :>> id = "a1b2c3d4-3908-4a10-9b20-d3908c0de055"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "Hardening Round 4 (independent critique, lens: FAILURE, RECOVERY & RESOURCE). ENGINE-INTERNAL, NO release. FIXED: F1 HIGH — the mount status FOLD (mountfsm/mountStatusSummary) had ZERO callers, so a silently offline/failed PULL mount showed green 'Fully synced' while the composed notes went stale; fix: effectiveLightPhase ESCALATES a resting primary to attention when a mount problem exists + paintLight surfaces which mount in the tooltip (finishes the #101 status-light fold). F2 MED — a failed mount never auto-recovered (the FSM retry was never dispatched); fix: a failed scope resets to detached after a backoff (MOUNT_FAILED_RETRY_MS=5min via failedAt) + a detached scope is started on ANY pass, so recovery + newly-added mounts take effect. F3 MED — onPullExhausted + onSkip were unwired, so a permanently-corrupt or over-size source file was silently missing; fix: wire both (notice + log). F4 MED — mounts never checked the SOURCE vault readiness (unlike the primary), so a source mid-reindex serving a partial manifest could drive a spurious delete-local; fix: a sourceReady() probe (source status()==='ready') gates the first-contact/reconnect pass — a not-ready source holds the mount OFFLINE, never reconciles a degraded manifest. CONFIRMED SAFE: fail-isolation (both layers), no unbounded hang (30s transport timeout), 503/degraded can't mass-delete (throw + emptyManifest/ratio/own DeleteRateGuard + onGuard), shared chunk cache bounded, per-mount isolation, no-session spins harmlessly, detached re-run bounded, pull read-only, removed/unmounting skipped mid-pass. NOTE (D0040 by-design): a pull mount lags ~60s (poll cadence). Guards: full client vitest 703 (new R4-F4 not-ready-source-held-offline test) + tsc + build clean; keel validate/guard green. Realizes nComposedVaults (hardening)."; }
        part mountHardeningR4DoDR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "a1b2c3d4-3908-4a10-9b20-d3908c0de056"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "5666fd6"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-08-08"; :>> judgedBy = "claudeOpus"; }
        #Covers dependency from sittingReview20260807b to mountHardeningR4;
        action mountHardeningR5;
        verification mountHardeningR5DoD : Test { :>> id = "a1b2c3d4-3909-4a10-9b20-d3909c0de057"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "Hardening Round 5 / FINAL (independent critique, lens: SECURITY + holistic 'what did R1-R4 miss'). ENGINE-INTERNAL, NO release. Critique verdict: SAFE TO SHIP for an on-device beta — NO exploitable breach (credential/.obsidian isolation, path-traversal containment, cross-vault non-leakage on push, token routing, per-scope isolation all verified solid + layered). FIXED: MED-1 — the `diverged` FSM state was UNREACHABLE (a mounted-folder conflict only logged → green light, violating honest-status); fix: MountRuntime.tookConflict drives the scope to `diverged` ('Needs review', surfaced on the light + card), cleared to live on a clean pass. MED-3 — one invalid hand-edited mount deactivated ALL mounts (activeMounts all-or-nothing) → primary re-absorbed their folders + uploaded source-derived content; fix: validMounts() returns the maximal valid non-overlapping SUBSET (a bad entry drops only itself). LOW-3 — switching the primary onto a mount's source → self-referential double-sync; fix: activeMounts excludes a mount of the current primary (auto-dormant after a switch). LOW-1 — MountedApi.putChunk wasn't pull-gated (the no-write-on-pull guarantee rested on reconcile, not the adapter); fix: putChunk hard-refuses on a pull mount. LOW-2 — ignorePatterns weren't applied inside mounts; fix: passed through. CONFIRMED SAFE (verified): credential/.obsidian exclusion airtight across every sink; no cross-vault content leak on push (commit chunks only the file's own bytes, never the shared cache); malicious-source traversal/huge/delete-flood/bad-chunk caught; token routing correct (encodeURIComponent'd /api/u/{owner}/{vault}); scope isolation; persistence round-trips; push/pull preview respects the boundary. MED-2 (moving a file out of a SYNC mount deletes it from the source — correct-but-surprising) recorded as issueMountCrossBoundaryMove (documented + rename/move-safety follow-up). Guards: full client vitest 703 (R2-F1 conflict test now asserts diverged→live) + tsc + build clean; keel validate/guard green. Realizes nComposedVaults (hardening — 5-round adversarial sweep complete)."; }
        part mountHardeningR5DoDR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "a1b2c3d4-3909-4a10-9b20-d3909c0de058"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "42b1449"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-08-08"; :>> judgedBy = "claudeOpus"; }
        #Covers dependency from sittingReview20260807b to mountHardeningR5;
        action mountHardeningR6;
        verification mountHardeningR6DoD : Test { :>> id = "a1b2c3d4-3910-4a10-9b20-d3910c0de059"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "Hardening Round 6 (independent critique, lens: MOBILE / PLATFORM-SPECIFIC). ENGINE-INTERNAL, NO release. FIXED: Med-1 — mounts were skipped on every IDLE (noop) primary poll (reconcileAllOnce returned at mode==='noop' before the reconcileMounts() call), so a source change didn't pull until the primary changed / the 15-min full scan / a reconnect (composed notes lag ~15min behind a green light; a non-dropping background→foreground resume didn't refresh mounts); fix: run reconcileMounts() on the noop branch too → mounts poll at the ~60s cadence (D0040). Med-2 — mobile OOM: the single-maxSyncMB refactor dropped the old 50-MiB mobile cap, so a mount (no streamed writer on mobile → buffers whole files ×FILE_CONCURRENCY) could buffer up to the 200-MiB desktop default and crash the WebView; fix: clamp the MOUNT's maxSyncBytes to 50 MiB on Platform.isMobile — a larger file is skipped + noticed (onSkip), never buffered (scoped to the mount; the primary user setting untouched). VERIFIED (specific points): MountedIo mirrors the base appendWrite capability (mobile→buffered fallback, not a broken stream); the mount io never enumerates .obsidian on mobile; mount base isolation holds; mounts get scan-skip + run reconcileDelta steady-state (no periodic whole-subtree re-hash). NOT fixed (un-verified / pre-existing, surfaced for on-device judgement, NOT silently changed): a possible iOS NFD-vs-NFC rel-key mismatch (may be masked by Obsidian's own normalization; a blind change risks a Linux regression) + mount deletes hard-unlinking on mobile where the adapter lacks trashLocal (pre-existing general behaviour). Both fixes are main.ts glue — verified by tsc + esbuild build + full client vitest 703 (no regression); the LIVE poll-cadence + mobile size-gate behaviour is NOT verified without an on-device run. Realizes nComposedVaults (hardening)."; }
        part mountHardeningR6DoDR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "a1b2c3d4-3910-4a10-9b20-d3910c0de060"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "ec6e661"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-08-10"; :>> judgedBy = "claudeOpus"; }
        #Covers dependency from sittingReview20260807b to mountHardeningR6;
        action mountHardeningR7;
        verification mountHardeningR7DoD : Test { :>> id = "a1b2c3d4-3911-4a10-9b20-d3911c0de061"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "Hardening Round 7 (independent critique, lens: PROTOCOL/WIRE + server-contract). ENGINE-INTERNAL, NO release. VERIFIED clean (traced): source responses get the SAME transport validation as the primary (malformed FileMeta throws pre-reconcile → offline, no disk mutation); retryBudget/onPullExhausted wired (hash-mismatch/404/reordered chunks → per-file skip + budget); commit CAS uses the source-global version + server-set author. FIXED: F1 MED — the mount checked source readiness but NOT apiVersion, and sessionToken persists after a version-mismatched primary connect, so a mount could poll a protocol-incompatible source (shape guards catch structural, not semantic, wire changes); fix: sourceReady() also runs versionVerdict(status().apiVersion, CLIENT_API_VERSION) and holds the mount OFFLINE on a mismatch. F2 LOW — fetchVerified checked hash but not size on the BUFFERED path (which mobile mounts always take; streamed path already checks both); fix: reject a FileMeta whose declared size disagrees from the assembled bytes (per-file isolated integrity hardening). NOT fixed (noted): F3 LOW — a hand-edited config dropping a shared source's owner mis-routes to your own namespace (UI never produces it; parseMounts can't distinguish a valid own-vault owner:'' from a dropped one; impact = your-own-other-vault, not a leak). Guards: full client vitest 703 (reconcile + mountsync + real-server e2e green — the size check didn't disturb happy paths) + tsc + build clean; F1 is main.ts glue + F2 mirrors an existing checked path — live behaviour un-verified without an on-device run against a version-mismatched/size-lying source. Realizes nComposedVaults (hardening)."; }
        part mountHardeningR7DoDR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "a1b2c3d4-3911-4a10-9b20-d3911c0de062"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "8550563"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-08-10"; :>> judgedBy = "claudeOpus"; }
        #Covers dependency from sittingReview20260807b to mountHardeningR7;
        // Backlog: full D0019 reset-detection for mounts (resolver for issueMountResetDetection, R2-F3 follow-up).
        action mountResetDetection;
        // Backlog: cross-boundary rename/move safety for sync mounts (resolver for issueMountCrossBoundaryMove, R5-MED-2 follow-up).
        action mountMoveSafety;
        verification sittingReview20260807b : Test { :>> id = "7a0d8f07-0807-4a10-9b20-a1b2c3d40809"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::confirmation; :>> procedureText = "Per-sitting human review (D0049) for the 2026-08-07 SECOND sitting — the composed-vaults Phase 2 engine-adapter work begun after the owner signed off the first 08-07 sitting and directed 'proceed'. Covers the composed-vaults (D0039) engine build, driven autonomously after the owner directed 'proceed until finished, I'll critique later': mountIoAdapters (the MountedIo/MountedApi two-sided prefix-translating adapters + the isDataPath data-only boundary), mountEngineCore (the MountRuntime structural base/state isolation + per-mount FSM + aggregate status fold), and mountEngine (the live sync loop + main.ts wiring — a second concurrent, POLL-DRIVEN [D0040], fail-isolated sync scope, DORMANT until a mount is configured). Each behaviour/data-touching increment went through an independent antagonistic security critique (+ a re-verify pass on the live glue) that caught + fixed real defects — a deleteFile data-only asymmetry, a normFolder round-trip bug, a fileMeta config-leak, a case-fold bypass, and — the big one — a HIGH A1 where the mount had reused the primary's filtered io (mount writes dropped + a reconnect would delete-remote the SOURCE vault), now fixed with a separate data-only mount io; issueMountBaseIsolation is resolved (per-mount base isolation structurally enforced + critique-re-confirmed). ALL engine-internal — no user-facing behaviour, NO release yet (the Phase 4 UI is the first consumer). HONESTLY PENDING: the owner has NOT reviewed any of this on-device; R1 stamped only on that explicit review. Each increment's closeOut/retro runs autonomously (D0049); this single confirmation is the sitting's human gate."; }
